{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:21:34", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-b8d465d0-c425-47d6-bb8c-dd0bef0f9aaf', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Foundation Infrastructure - Establish core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security including frequent coherent commits, branch-based development, state persistence & recovery, and secrets management",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Lxrp6Astas7yCk69DKRbfv', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Lxrp6Astas7yCk69DKRbfv', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: UI Readability Fix for Improve Page\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted remediation architecture** for fixing text readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach focuses on CSS specificity corrections and conditional styling improvements rather than a major architectural redesign.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-level styling fix with cascading CSS improvements\\n**Rationale**: This is a focused bug fix that requires minimal changes to preserve existing functionality while solving the specific contrast problem. A surgical approach ensures no unintended side effects.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n**No new technologies required** - this fix works within the existing stack:\\n\\n### Frontend (Existing)\\n- **React** - Component framework (already in use)\\n- **Bootstrap 5** - CSS framework with built-in color system (leveraging existing theme)\\n- **CSS-in-JS/Inline Styles** - Current styling approach in the component\\n\\n### Why This Approach\\n- **Minimal Risk**: Works with existing technology and patterns\\n- **Fast Implementation**: No new dependencies or learning curve\\n- **Maintainable**: Uses Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes for consistency\\n- **Tested**: Bootstrap\'s color combinations are accessibility-tested\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered:**\\n- CSS Modules: Overkill for a single component fix\\n- Styled Components: Would require major refactoring\\n- New CSS Framework: Unnecessary complexity for a readability fix\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Core Component\\n**SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx**\\n- **Current State**: Contains conditional styling that causes contrast issues\\n- **Responsibility**: Display performance analytics with proper text contrast\\n- **Fix Strategy**: Update styling logic to ensure text colors adapt with background changes\\n\\n### Styling Architecture\\n```\\nSelfImprovementDashboard\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Normal Mode Styling (light backgrounds)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-light, text-dark)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (semantic colors with proper text)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (standard contrast)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 \\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling (dark/danger backgrounds)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-danger, text-white)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (light variants with dark text)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (inverted contrast)\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n```\\nUser Interaction \\u2192 Mode State Change \\u2192 Conditional Styling Logic \\u2192 DOM Update \\u2192 Visual Rendering\\n```\\nNo changes to data flow - only styling application logic.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n**Files to Modify:**\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx  [PRIMARY TARGET]\\n```\\n\\n**Additional Files (if needed):**\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 dashboard-overrides.css  [IF NEEDED - for complex overrides]\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeHelpers.js  [IF NEEDED - for styling logic extraction]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**No database changes required** - this is purely a presentation layer fix.\\n\\n**State Management:**\\n- Existing component state (bumpers mode, performance data) remains unchanged\\n- Only CSS class application logic needs modification\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API changes required** - this fix is entirely frontend styling.\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Process\\n1. **Local Development**: Test fixes in development server\\n2. **Visual Testing**: Verify contrast in both light and dark modes\\n3. **Accessibility Testing**: Use browser dev tools to verify WCAG compliance\\n4. **Cross-Browser Testing**: Ensure fixes work in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n### Deployment\\n- **Type**: Frontend-only deployment\\n- **Risk Level**: Low (isolated component changes)\\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Git revert of specific styling changes\\n- **Testing Required**: Visual regression testing\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\nNo environment-specific configuration needed - styles apply universally.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Manual test cases:\\n1. Load Improve page in normal mode\\n   \\u2192 Verify all text is readable against backgrounds\\n2. Enable \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode  \\n   \\u2192 Verify danger theme maintains text contrast\\n3. Test responsive breakpoints\\n   \\u2192 Ensure readability on mobile/tablet/desktop\\n```\\n\\n### Automated Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Accessibility tests (if jest-axe available):\\ndescribe(\'SelfImprovementDashboard Accessibility\', () => {\\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in normal mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test WCAG compliance\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in bumpers off mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test danger theme compliance\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Browser Testing\\n- **Chrome**: Primary development browser\\n- **Firefox**: Secondary testing\\n- **Safari**: macOS compatibility\\n- **Edge**: Windows compatibility\\n\\n## Specific Technical Implementation\\n\\n### Bootstrap Color Strategy\\n```jsx\\n// Current problematic pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-muted\\">Problem text</span> // This creates dark on dark\\n</Card>\\n\\n// Fixed pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-light\\">Readable text</span>\\n</Card>\\n```\\n\\n### Conditional Styling Logic\\n```jsx\\nconst getTextClass = (isDangerMode, baseClass) => {\\n  if (isDangerMode) {\\n    return baseClass.includes(\'dark\') ? \'text-white\' : \'text-light\';\\n  }\\n  return baseClass.includes(\'light\') ? \'text-dark\' : \'text-white\';\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Option 1: Complete CSS Framework Migration\\n**Rejected**: Too much risk for a simple contrast fix\\n\\n### Option 2: Custom Design System\\n**Rejected**: Overkill - Bootstrap\'s accessibility features solve this when used correctly\\n\\n### Option 3: JavaScript-based Theme Switching\\n**Rejected**: Adds complexity when CSS classes can solve the issue\\n\\n### Option 4: CSS Variables for Dynamic Theming\\n**Considered**: Good for future scalability, but unnecessary for this focused fix\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Breaking Existing Visual Design\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes\\n- Test both modes thoroughly\\n- Take screenshots for before/after comparison\\n\\n### Risk 2: CSS Specificity Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use inline styles for high specificity when needed\\n- Follow existing patterns in the codebase\\n- Test in actual browser environment\\n\\n### Risk 3: Performance Impact\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- No new CSS files or frameworks\\n- Minimal additional class computations\\n- No impact on bundle size\\n\\n### Risk 4: Cross-Browser Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use standard Bootstrap classes (well-tested across browsers)\\n- Test in multiple browsers\\n- Avoid custom CSS properties that might not be supported\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Design Questions for User Review\\n1. **Color Preference**: Should danger mode use red backgrounds with white text, or prefer orange/yellow for better accessibility?\\n2. **Badge Styling**: For dark badges, prefer white text or switch to light-colored badges with dark text?\\n3. **Table Styling**: In dark mode, prefer inverted table colors or maintain current table style with better text contrast?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input\\n1. **Approach**: Pure inline styling vs. conditional CSS classes?\\n2. **Scope**: Fix only the reported component or audit entire application for similar issues?\\n3. **Testing**: Include automated accessibility tests or rely on manual verification?\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Immediate Fix (1-2 hours)\\n- Identify and fix the most critical contrast issues\\n- Focus on badges and card text\\n- Test both normal and danger modes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Comprehensive Audit (2-3 hours)\\n- Review all text elements in the component\\n- Ensure WCAG compliance\\n- Add consistent styling patterns\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing and Validation (1 hour)\\n- Cross-browser testing\\n- Accessibility validation\\n- User acceptance testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Contrast Ratio**: All text meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large)\\n2. **Visual Verification**: User confirms readability issues are resolved\\n3. **No Regression**: All existing functionality works unchanged\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable impact on page load or rendering performance\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **User Approval**: Confirm this architectural approach before implementation\\n2. **Development**: Implement the CSS fixes following this plan\\n3. **Testing**: Execute the testing strategy outlined above\\n4. **Deployment**: Deploy with the low-risk strategy described\\n\\nThis architecture provides a focused, low-risk solution that addresses the specific readability problem while maintaining system stability and existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NPSdfQaJP5CrYPWV2Zhe64', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NPSdfQaJP5CrYPWV2Zhe64', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\\n\\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\\n\\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\\n\\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\\n\\n## Target Users\\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\\n\\n## Constraints\\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\\n- Mobile application interface\\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\\n- Frequent commits system\\n- Branch-based development\\n- State persistence\\n- Secrets management\\n\\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \\n- CI/CD agent\\n- Cost tracking\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Code review automation\\n\\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\\n- Knowledge repository agent\\n- Agent performance learning\\n- Multi-provider routing\\n- Self-healing capabilities\\n\\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\\n- Web dashboard\\n- Integration capabilities\\n- Advanced collaboration features\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \\n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Vy3WknaMuMa7vhCXm9HFkE', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Frontend Tasks - Foundation Infrastructure\n\n## Milestone Overview\nEstablish core frontend infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security including frequent coherent commits, branch-based development, state persistence & recovery, and secrets management.\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Core Infrastructure Components\n\n#### Task 1: Project State Management Service\n**Description**: Create a frontend service to manage project state, task tracking, and milestone progress\n**Acceptance Criteria**: \n- Service can create, read, update project state\n- Tracks tasks with status, assignments, and dependencies\n- Maintains milestone progress with completion metrics\n- Provides state persistence and recovery capabilities\n**Dependencies**: None (foundational)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 2: Git Workflow Management Interface\n**Description**: Build UI components for git branch management, commit history, and merge operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Display current branch status and commit history\n- Allow branch creation, switching, and deletion through UI\n- Show merge conflicts and resolution options\n- Visualize branch topology and relationships\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (project state)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n#### Task 3: Cost Tracking Dashboard Components\n**Description**: Create components to display API costs, usage metrics, and budget tracking\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Real-time cost display with provider breakdown\n- Budget alerts and threshold warnings\n- Historical usage charts and trends\n- Export capabilities for cost reports\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (project state)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 4: State Persistence Service\n**Description**: Implement frontend service for checkpoint creation, state backup, and recovery operations\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Create and restore application state checkpoints\n- Handle interrupted operations gracefully\n- Provide manual and automatic backup triggers\n- Display recovery options when state corruption detected\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (project state)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 5: Secrets Management Interface\n**Description**: Build secure UI for managing API keys, credentials, and configuration secrets\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Secure form for adding/editing API credentials\n- Masked display of sensitive information\n- Validation of credential formats and permissions\n- Audit trail of credential access and modifications\n**Dependencies**: None (security critical)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n### Agent Coordination Components\n\n#### Task 6: Agent Status Monitor\n**Description**: Create real-time display of agent execution status, progress, and health metrics\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Live status updates for active agents\n- Progress indicators for long-running tasks\n- Error state display with diagnostic information\n- Agent performance metrics and success rates\n**Dependencies**: Task 1 (project state)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 7: Agent Communication Panel\n**Description**: Build interface for inter-agent messaging, coordination, and conflict resolution\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Display agent-to-agent communication logs\n- Show coordination events and handoffs\n- Provide manual intervention options for conflicts\n- Visual representation of agent collaboration workflows\n**Dependencies**: Task 6 (agent status)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n#### Task 8: Commit Attribution Display\n**Description**: Create components to show agent authorship, commit quality, and automated commit formatting\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Display commits with proper agent attribution\n- Show commit quality scores and metrics\n- Format commit messages according to standards\n- Link commits to originating tasks and agents\n**Dependencies**: Task 2 (git workflow)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n### User Experience Components\n\n#### Task 9: Navigation and Layout Framework\n**Description**: Build responsive navigation system and page layout components\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Responsive sidebar navigation with collapsible sections\n- Header with breadcrumb navigation and user context\n- Main content area with proper spacing and typography\n- Mobile-friendly responsive design\n**Dependencies**: None (foundational)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n#### Task 10: Form Components Library\n**Description**: Create reusable form components with validation, error handling, and accessibility\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Input components with built-in validation\n- Form containers with error state management\n- Accessible form labels and ARIA attributes\n- Consistent styling matching design system\n**Dependencies**: Task 9 (layout framework)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 11: Data Visualization Components\n**Description**: Build charts, graphs, and metrics display components for dashboards\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Line charts for cost and performance trends\n- Progress bars and completion indicators\n- Real-time updating charts with smooth animations\n- Responsive design for different screen sizes\n**Dependencies**: Task 9 (layout framework)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 12: Modal and Dialog System\n**Description**: Create modal dialogs for confirmations, forms, and detailed views\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Reusable modal component with different sizes\n- Form modals for editing configurations\n- Confirmation dialogs for destructive actions\n- Accessibility features (focus management, escape key)\n**Dependencies**: Task 9 (layout framework)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n### Integration and API Components\n\n#### Task 13: API Client Service\n**Description**: Build frontend service for backend communication with error handling and retry logic\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- RESTful API client with standardized error handling\n- Automatic retry logic for failed requests\n- Request/response logging for debugging\n- Authentication token management\n**Dependencies**: Task 5 (secrets management)\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 14: WebSocket Connection Manager\n**Description**: Implement real-time communication service for live updates and agent events\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Persistent WebSocket connection with reconnection logic\n- Event-driven updates for agent status and progress\n- Connection status indicators\n- Message queuing for offline scenarios\n**Dependencies**: Task 13 (API client)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n#### Task 15: Notification System\n**Description**: Create toast notifications, alerts, and status indicators for user feedback\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Toast notifications for success/error/info messages\n- System-wide alert banners for important status\n- Progress notifications for long operations\n- Dismissible notifications with auto-timeout\n**Dependencies**: Task 9 (layout framework)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n### Testing and Quality Components\n\n#### Task 16: Component Testing Framework\n**Description**: Set up testing infrastructure for React components with mocking and assertions\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Jest and React Testing Library configuration\n- Component test utilities and helpers\n- Mock services for isolated component testing\n- Test coverage reporting and thresholds\n**Dependencies**: All component tasks\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n#### Task 17: Integration Testing Suite\n**Description**: Create end-to-end testing for user workflows and component interactions\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Cypress or Playwright test configuration\n- Critical user journey test scenarios\n- API integration testing with mock backends\n- Visual regression testing capabilities\n**Dependencies**: Task 16 (component testing)\n**Complexity**: Complex\n\n#### Task 18: Error Boundary Implementation\n**Description**: Add error boundaries for graceful failure handling and user error reporting\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Component-level error boundaries with fallback UI\n- Global error boundary for unhandled exceptions\n- Error reporting to logging service\n- User-friendly error messages with recovery options\n**Dependencies**: Task 9 (layout framework)\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n## Task Dependencies\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    T1[Project State Service] --> T2[Git Workflow Interface]\n    T1 --> T3[Cost Tracking Dashboard]\n    T1 --> T4[State Persistence Service]\n    T1 --> T6[Agent Status Monitor]\n    \n    T5[Secrets Management] --> T13[API Client Service]\n    T6 --> T7[Agent Communication Panel]\n    T2 --> T8[Commit Attribution Display]\n    \n    T9[Navigation Layout] --> T10[Form Components]\n    T9 --> T11[Data Visualization]\n    T9 --> T12[Modal System]\n    T9 --> T15[Notification System]\n    T9 --> T18[Error Boundaries]\n    \n    T13 --> T14[WebSocket Manager]\n    \n    T10 --> T16[Component Testing]\n    T11 --> T16\n    T12 --> T16\n    T16 --> T17[Integration Testing]\n```\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Tasks 1, 5, 9)\n- Project State Management Service\n- Secrets Management Interface\n- Navigation and Layout Framework\n\n### Phase 2: Core Infrastructure (Tasks 2, 3, 4, 13)\n- Git Workflow Management Interface\n- Cost Tracking Dashboard Components\n- State Persistence Service\n- API Client Service\n\n### Phase 3: User Experience (Tasks 6, 10, 11, 12, 15, 18)\n- Agent Status Monitor\n- Form Components Library\n- Data Visualization Components\n- Modal and Dialog System\n- Notification System\n- Error Boundary Implementation\n\n### Phase 4: Advanced Features (Tasks 7, 8, 14)\n- Agent Communication Panel\n- Commit Attribution Display\n- WebSocket Connection Manager\n\n### Phase 5: Quality Assurance (Tasks 16, 17)\n- Component Testing Framework\n- Integration Testing Suite\n\n## Technical Architecture\n\n### State Management\n- React Context API for global state (project, user, settings)\n- Local component state for UI interactions\n- Persistent state service for checkpoints and recovery\n\n### Styling Approach\n- Tailwind CSS for utility-first styling\n- CSS Modules for component-specific styles\n- Design system tokens for consistent theming\n\n### API Integration\n- Axios for HTTP requests with interceptors\n- WebSocket for real-time updates\n- Error boundary pattern for resilient API handling\n\n### Testing Strategy\n- Unit tests for all utility functions and services\n- Component tests for UI behavior and interactions\n- Integration tests for critical user workflows\n- Visual regression tests for UI consistency\n\n## Complexity Summary\n- Simple Tasks: 4 (Tasks 8, 9, 12, 15, 18)\n- Medium Tasks: 8 (Tasks 1, 3, 4, 6, 10, 11, 13, 16)\n- Complex Tasks: 6 (Tasks 2, 5, 7, 14, 17)\n\n**Total Estimated Tasks: 18**\n**Implementation Timeline: 4-5 sprints**'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Vy3WknaMuMa7vhCXm9HFkE', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260114_232134.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1_20260114_232134.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 95.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches,