{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:21:40", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-d3d8f5b2-3228-4d69-869e-fcaf4b6e20c2', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Future Features Implementation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019U9ddEXzth6CSo3F5uwWCE', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019U9ddEXzth6CSo3F5uwWCE', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\\n\\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\\n\\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\\n\\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\\n\\n## Target Users\\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\\n\\n## Constraints\\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\\n- Mobile application interface\\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\\n- Frequent commits system\\n- Branch-based development\\n- State persistence\\n- Secrets management\\n\\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \\n- CI/CD agent\\n- Cost tracking\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Code review automation\\n\\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\\n- Knowledge repository agent\\n- Agent performance learning\\n- Multi-provider routing\\n- Self-healing capabilities\\n\\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\\n- Web dashboard\\n- Integration capabilities\\n- Advanced collaboration features\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \\n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01QrMgwxbrFPFQu7sc8f93hw', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': "# Future Features Implementation - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nImplementing 22 advanced features for the Ensemble multi-agent development platform, focusing on workflow improvements, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience enhancements.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Foundation Infrastructure (Weeks 1-3)\n**Objective**: Establish core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Enhanced git commit system with agent attribution\n- Branch-based development workflow \n- State persistence and recovery mechanisms\n- Secrets management framework\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management  \n3. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\n4. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Agents automatically create meaningful commits with attribution\n- Branch creation/switching works seamlessly with agent coordination\n- System can recover from interruptions using checkpoints\n- All secrets are encrypted and accessed through secure vault\n- Zero regressions in existing functionality\n- Full test coverage for new git and persistence tools\n\n**Dependencies**: Existing git tooling, database persistence layer\n\n### Milestone 2: Quality Assurance & Monitoring (Weeks 4-6)\n**Objective**: Implement automated quality checks and comprehensive monitoring infrastructure\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Continuous integration agent for automated testing\n- Cost tracking and budgeting system\n- Performance metrics collection and dashboard\n- Automated code review capabilities\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n5. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\n6. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\n7. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\n8. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- CI agent runs comprehensive tests on all commits\n- Real-time cost tracking with configurable budget alerts\n- Performance dashboard shows agent success rates and efficiency metrics\n- Code review agent identifies quality issues before merge\n- All quality checks integrate with branch workflow\n- Cost tracking accuracy within 5% of actual usage\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (branch workflow), LLM provider APIs for cost data\n\n### Milestone 3: Intelligent Coordination (Weeks 7-9)\n**Objective**: Enable advanced agent coordination and knowledge management\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Knowledge repository for project context\n- Concurrent agent execution system\n- Agent collaboration protocols\n- Multi-provider LLM routing\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n9. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\n10. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\n11. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\n12. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Knowledge repository maintains comprehensive project context\n- Multiple agents can work on different branches simultaneously\n- Agents can communicate and coordinate across branches\n- LLM routing optimizes model selection based on task requirements\n- No conflicts between concurrent agent sessions\n- Knowledge base integrates with all agent decisions\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (branch system), Milestone 2 (monitoring infrastructure)\n\n### Milestone 4: Advanced Intelligence (Weeks 10-12)\n**Objective**: Implement self-optimizing and self-healing capabilities\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Agent performance learning system\n- Self-healing failure recovery\n- Comprehensive audit trail\n- Agent composition engine\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n13. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\n14. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\n15. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\n16. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- System learns from agent performance and optimizes future assignments\n- Automatic failure detection with strategy adjustment\n- Complete audit trail of all agent actions and decisions\n- Automated pipeline generation based on task complexity\n- Performance improvements measurable over baseline\n- Self-healing reduces manual intervention by 80%\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (performance metrics), Milestone 3 (agent coordination)\n\n### Milestone 5: User Experience & Integration (Weeks 13-15)\n**Objective**: Create interactive interfaces and external integrations\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Interactive web dashboard\n- Documentation generator agent\n- Slack/Discord integration\n- Docker-based execution environment\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n17. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\n18. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\n19. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\n20. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Web dashboard provides real-time visibility and control\n- Automated documentation generation for all projects\n- Slack/Discord integration supports common commands\n- Containerized execution improves isolation and reliability\n- Dashboard supports manual intervention during execution\n- Generated documentation meets quality standards\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (metrics dashboard), Milestone 4 (audit trail)\n\n### Milestone 6: Future Technologies (Weeks 16-18)\n**Objective**: Implement advanced distributed capabilities (Optional/Future)\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Distributed agent execution system\n- Voice interface prototype\n\n**Features Implemented**:\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Agents can execute across multiple machines\n- Voice interface supports basic project commands\n- Distributed execution maintains consistency\n- Voice interface integrates with dashboard\n\n**Dependencies**: All previous milestones, additional infrastructure for distribution\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### High Risk Items\n- **Concurrent agent coordination**: Complex locking and conflict resolution\n- **State persistence reliability**: Critical for recovery scenarios\n- **Cost tracking accuracy**: Must be precise for budget management\n\n### Medium Risk Items  \n- **Performance impact of monitoring**: New features shouldn't slow system\n- **Security of secrets management**: Must follow enterprise security practices\n- **Integration complexity**: Multiple new systems interacting\n\n### Mitigation Strategies\n- Comprehensive testing at each milestone\n- Rollback capabilities for all new features\n- Security review for credential handling\n- Performance benchmarking throughout implementation\n- Incremental feature activation with feature flags\n\n## Dependencies & Prerequisites\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture\n- Git repository and branch management\n- Database/persistence infrastructure  \n- LLM provider API access\n- Container runtime environment (for later milestones)\n- Web framework for dashboard development\n\n## Resource Requirements\n- Development team familiar with Ensemble architecture\n- Database administrator for persistence setup\n- Security engineer for secrets management review\n- DevOps engineer for CI/CD and containerization\n- UI/UX support for dashboard development\n\n## Success Metrics\n- All HIGH PRIORITY features (7 features) fully implemented\n- Zero regressions in existing functionality\n- Cost tracking within 5% accuracy\n- 80% reduction in manual intervention through self-healing\n- Performance improvements measurable in agent efficiency\n- Complete test coverage for all new features\n- User documentation for all implemented features\n\n## Communication Plan\n- Weekly milestone reviews\n- Daily standup for active development phases\n- Security and architecture reviews at milestone boundaries\n- Stakeholder demos at milestone completion\n- Risk assessment updates as needed"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01QrMgwxbrFPFQu7sc8f93hw', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_231817.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_231817.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01492LGrE2GMAuYUi1vPRr8P', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Future Features Implementation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01492LGrE2GMAuYUi1vPRr8P', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Td1U5EqLinxPP1seJF7Dwu', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Future Features Implementation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Td1U5EqLinxPP1seJF7Dwu', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PDwVDrTsYFAgD5Az1TT8hJ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PDwVDrTsYFAgD5Az1TT8hJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: UI Readability Fix for Improve Page\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted remediation architecture** for fixing text readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach focuses on CSS specificity corrections and conditional styling improvements rather than a major architectural redesign.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-level styling fix with cascading CSS improvements\\n**Rationale**: This is a focused bug fix that requires minimal changes to preserve existing functionality while solving the specific contrast problem. A surgical approach ensures no unintended side effects.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n**No new technologies required** - this fix works within the existing stack:\\n\\n### Frontend (Existing)\\n- **React** - Component framework (already in use)\\n- **Bootstrap 5** - CSS framework with built-in color system (leveraging existing theme)\\n- **CSS-in-JS/Inline Styles** - Current styling approach in the component\\n\\n### Why This Approach\\n- **Minimal Risk**: Works with existing technology and patterns\\n- **Fast Implementation**: No new dependencies or learning curve\\n- **Maintainable**: Uses Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes for consistency\\n- **Tested**: Bootstrap\'s color combinations are accessibility-tested\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered:**\\n- CSS Modules: Overkill for a single component fix\\n- Styled Components: Would require major refactoring\\n- New CSS Framework: Unnecessary complexity for a readability fix\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Core Component\\n**SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx**\\n- **Current State**: Contains conditional styling that causes contrast issues\\n- **Responsibility**: Display performance analytics with proper text contrast\\n- **Fix Strategy**: Update styling logic to ensure text colors adapt with background changes\\n\\n### Styling Architecture\\n```\\nSelfImprovementDashboard\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Normal Mode Styling (light backgrounds)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-light, text-dark)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (semantic colors with proper text)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (standard contrast)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 \\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling (dark/danger backgrounds)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-danger, text-white)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (light variants with dark text)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (inverted contrast)\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n```\\nUser Interaction \\u2192 Mode State Change \\u2192 Conditional Styling Logic \\u2192 DOM Update \\u2192 Visual Rendering\\n```\\nNo changes to data flow - only styling application logic.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n**Files to Modify:**\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx  [PRIMARY TARGET]\\n```\\n\\n**Additional Files (if needed):**\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 dashboard-overrides.css  [IF NEEDED - for complex overrides]\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeHelpers.js  [IF NEEDED - for styling logic extraction]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**No database changes required** - this is purely a presentation layer fix.\\n\\n**State Management:**\\n- Existing component state (bumpers mode, performance data) remains unchanged\\n- Only CSS class application logic needs modification\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API changes required** - this fix is entirely frontend styling.\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Process\\n1. **Local Development**: Test fixes in development server\\n2. **Visual Testing**: Verify contrast in both light and dark modes\\n3. **Accessibility Testing**: Use browser dev tools to verify WCAG compliance\\n4. **Cross-Browser Testing**: Ensure fixes work in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n### Deployment\\n- **Type**: Frontend-only deployment\\n- **Risk Level**: Low (isolated component changes)\\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Git revert of specific styling changes\\n- **Testing Required**: Visual regression testing\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\nNo environment-specific configuration needed - styles apply universally.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Manual test cases:\\n1. Load Improve page in normal mode\\n   \\u2192 Verify all text is readable against backgrounds\\n2. Enable \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode  \\n   \\u2192 Verify danger theme maintains text contrast\\n3. Test responsive breakpoints\\n   \\u2192 Ensure readability on mobile/tablet/desktop\\n```\\n\\n### Automated Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Accessibility tests (if jest-axe available):\\ndescribe(\'SelfImprovementDashboard Accessibility\', () => {\\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in normal mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test WCAG compliance\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in bumpers off mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test danger theme compliance\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Browser Testing\\n- **Chrome**: Primary development browser\\n- **Firefox**: Secondary testing\\n- **Safari**: macOS compatibility\\n- **Edge**: Windows compatibility\\n\\n## Specific Technical Implementation\\n\\n### Bootstrap Color Strategy\\n```jsx\\n// Current problematic pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-muted\\">Problem text</span> // This creates dark on dark\\n</Card>\\n\\n// Fixed pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-light\\">Readable text</span>\\n</Card>\\n```\\n\\n### Conditional Styling Logic\\n```jsx\\nconst getTextClass = (isDangerMode, baseClass) => {\\n  if (isDangerMode) {\\n    return baseClass.includes(\'dark\') ? \'text-white\' : \'text-light\';\\n  }\\n  return baseClass.includes(\'light\') ? \'text-dark\' : \'text-white\';\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Option 1: Complete CSS Framework Migration\\n**Rejected**: Too much risk for a simple contrast fix\\n\\n### Option 2: Custom Design System\\n**Rejected**: Overkill - Bootstrap\'s accessibility features solve this when used correctly\\n\\n### Option 3: JavaScript-based Theme Switching\\n**Rejected**: Adds complexity when CSS classes can solve the issue\\n\\n### Option 4: CSS Variables for Dynamic Theming\\n**Considered**: Good for future scalability, but unnecessary for this focused fix\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Breaking Existing Visual Design\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes\\n- Test both modes thoroughly\\n- Take screenshots for before/after comparison\\n\\n### Risk 2: CSS Specificity Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use inline styles for high specificity when needed\\n- Follow existing patterns in the codebase\\n- Test in actual browser environment\\n\\n### Risk 3: Performance Impact\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- No new CSS files or frameworks\\n- Minimal additional class computations\\n- No impact on bundle size\\n\\n### Risk 4: Cross-Browser Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use standard Bootstrap classes (well-tested across browsers)\\n- Test in multiple browsers\\n- Avoid custom CSS properties that might not be supported\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Design Questions for User Review\\n1. **Color Preference**: Should danger mode use red backgrounds with white text, or prefer orange/yellow for better accessibility?\\n2. **Badge Styling**: For dark badges, prefer white text or switch to light-colored badges with dark text?\\n3. **Table Styling**: In dark mode, prefer inverted table colors or maintain current table style with better text contrast?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input\\n1. **Approach**: Pure inline styling vs. conditional CSS classes?\\n2. **Scope**: Fix only the reported component or audit entire application for similar issues?\\n3. **Testing**: Include automated accessibility tests or rely on manual verification?\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Immediate Fix (1-2 hours)\\n- Identify and fix the most critical contrast issues\\n- Focus on badges and card text\\n- Test both normal and danger modes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Comprehensive Audit (2-3 hours)\\n- Review all text elements in the component\\n- Ensure WCAG compliance\\n- Add consistent styling patterns\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing and Validation (1 hour)\\n- Cross-browser testing\\n- Accessibility validation\\n- User acceptance testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Contrast Ratio**: All text meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large)\\n2. **Visual Verification**: User confirms readability issues are resolved\\n3. **No Regression**: All existing functionality works unchanged\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable impact on page load or rendering performance\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **User Approval**: Confirm this architectural approach before implementation\\n2. **Development**: Implement the CSS fixes following this plan\\n3. **Testing**: Execute the testing strategy outlined above\\n4. **Deployment**: Deploy with the low-risk strategy described\\n\\nThis architecture provides a focused, low-risk solution that addresses the specific readability problem while maintaining system stability and existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LcEzSoVS7Dhg8Gdtzeb8ox', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Foundation Infrastructure - Establish core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security including frequent coherent commits, branch-based development, state persistence & recovery, and secrets management', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LcEzSoVS7Dhg8Gdtzeb8ox', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 10, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Database Schema & Migrations \\u2192 State Persistence System", "Database Schema & Migrations \\u2192 Secrets Management Service", "Database Schema & Migrations \\u2192 Project Context Database", "Database Schema & Migrations \\u2192 Authentication & Authorization System", "Authentication & Authorization System \\u2192 API Gateway & Routing", "API Gateway & Routing \\u2192 Enhanced Git Workflow API", "API Gateway & Routing \\u2192 Cost Tracking API", "API Gateway & Routing \\u2192 Performance Metrics Collection", "Performance Metrics Collection \\u2192 Agent Communication Protocol Backend", "State Persistence System \\u2192 Agent Communication Protocol Backend"], "message": "Successfully analyzed architecture and requirements to create 10 backend tasks for Foundation Infrastructure milestone. Tasks cover core systems needed for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security including database schema, authentication, API gateway, state persistence, secrets management, cost tracking, and performance metrics. All tasks include specific acceptance criteria and are organized by dependency order for efficient implementation."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ECeEteCsi3qAnQ4WsVQtDs', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Foundation Infrastructure - Establish core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security including frequent coherent commits, branch-based development, state persistence & recovery, and secrets management', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ECeEteCsi3qAnQ4WsVQtDs', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 18, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1 (Project State Service) \\u2192 Tasks 2, 3, 4, 6", "Task 5 (Secrets Management) \\u2192 Task 13", "Task 6 (Agent Status) \\u2192 Task 7", "Task 2 (Git Workflow) \\u2192 Task 8", "Task 9 (Layout Framework) \\u2192 Tasks 10, 11, 12, 15, 18", "Task 13 (API Client) \\u2192 Task 14", "Tasks 10, 11, 12 \\u2192 Task 16", "Task 16 (Component Testing) \\u2192 Task 17"], "message": "Successfully identified 18 frontend tasks for Foundation Infrastructure milestone. Tasks organized into 5 phases covering core infrastructure (state management, git workflows, cost tracking), user experience components (navigation, forms, visualizations), integration services (API client, WebSocket), and quality assurance (testing frameworks). Ready for TDD Coordinator implementation."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 91.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.0\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I successfully executed the complete project lifecycle: read requirements, created milestone plan, spawned System Architect for architecture, coordinated with Backend/Frontend/Test Coordinators for ta...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
