{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:22:06", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-7960a4b6-f191-434c-b058-9eb4c1461dbc', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Fix Improve Page UI Readability"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FcdMVWLLM6DwPa1pfQobqm', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FcdMVWLLM6DwPa1pfQobqm', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Readability Fix - Improve Page\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n**Project Name:** Fix Improve Page UI Readability  \\n**Type:** Bug Fix  \\n**Priority:** High  \\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nThe user has reported that text on the \\"Improve\\" page (SelfImprovementDashboard component) is almost impossible to read due to black text appearing on dark backgrounds, creating poor contrast and accessibility issues.\\n\\n## Current State Analysis\\nAfter examining the SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx component, several potential readability issues were identified:\\n\\n1. **Dynamic Background Colors with Fixed Text**: Card components use `bg=\\"dark\\"` with `text=\\"white\\"` but some styling may override this\\n2. **\\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling**: When auto-apply is enabled, the interface switches to danger/dark themes that may have contrast issues\\n3. **Badge Components**: Multiple Badge components with `bg=\\"dark\\"` that may have poor text contrast\\n4. **Table Text in Dark Containers**: Tables inside cards with dark styling may have visibility issues\\n5. **Modal and Form Controls**: Form elements may not have proper contrast in dark mode contexts\\n\\n## Root Cause\\nThe component uses conditional styling that changes background colors to dark variants (danger, dark themes) when certain modes are active, but text color adjustments may not be properly applied, resulting in dark text on dark backgrounds.\\n\\n## Solution Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n1. **Fix Text Contrast**: Ensure all text has sufficient contrast ratio (minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text) against its background\\n2. **Maintain Visual Hierarchy**: Preserve the current design intent while improving readability\\n3. **Consistent Theming**: Ensure text color properly adapts when background colors change\\n4. **Accessibility Compliance**: Meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards for color contrast\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n1. **CSS/Style Fixes**: Update inline styles and className assignments to ensure proper text colors\\n2. **Bootstrap Theme Compatibility**: Ensure fixes work with Bootstrap\'s color system\\n3. **Responsive Design**: Maintain readability across all screen sizes\\n4. **Mode-Specific Styling**: Properly handle \\"Bumpers Off\\" danger theme and normal theme\\n\\n### Specific Areas to Address\\n1. **Badge Text Colors**: Ensure text on dark badges is white/light colored\\n2. **Card Text in Dark Themes**: Verify text color in danger/dark themed cards\\n3. **Table Text**: Ensure table content is readable in all contexts\\n4. **Form Controls**: Verify form text and labels have proper contrast\\n5. **Alert Text**: Ensure alert content maintains readability\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Visual Verification**: All text on the Improve page should be clearly readable\\n2. **Contrast Testing**: All text should pass WCAG contrast ratio requirements\\n3. **No Regression**: Current functionality and visual design should be preserved\\n4. **Cross-Browser Compatibility**: Fixes should work consistently across browsers\\n\\n## Scope\\n**In Scope:**\\n- Fix text contrast issues in SelfImprovementDashboard component\\n- Update CSS/styling to ensure proper text visibility\\n- Test readability in both normal and \\"Bumpers Off\\" modes\\n\\n**Out of Scope:**\\n- Major design changes or component restructuring\\n- Changes to other pages or components\\n- New feature development\\n- Backend modifications\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The issue is primarily in the SelfImprovementDashboard component (confirmed via file search)\\n- Bootstrap\'s built-in color classes should provide proper contrast when used correctly\\n- The current design intent should be preserved while improving readability\\n- This is a frontend-only fix requiring no backend changes\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Must maintain existing functionality\\n- Should not break responsive design\\n- Must work with existing Bootstrap theme\\n- Should follow existing code patterns and conventions\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n1. All text on the Improve page should be clearly visible and readable\\n2. Text contrast should meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards\\n3. Functionality should remain unchanged\\n4. Visual design should be preserved while improving accessibility\\n5. Both normal mode and \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode should have proper text contrast"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LuU1h8gz2jRN57DZyBSsZW', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Fix Improve Page UI Readability - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\n**Project Name:** Fix Improve Page UI Readability  \n**Type:** Bug Fix  \n**Priority:** High  \n**Estimated Duration:** 1-2 days\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Analysis and Planning (2-4 hours)\n**Objective:** Thoroughly analyze the SelfImprovementDashboard component to identify all contrast issues and plan the fixes.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Detailed analysis of contrast issues in the component\n- Architecture review for proper styling approach\n- Task breakdown for frontend fixes\n- Test plan for verifying contrast compliance\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- All contrast issues identified and documented\n- Clear understanding of Bootstrap theming implications\n- Specific fix strategy defined for each problem area\n- Dependencies and risks assessed\n\n**Dependencies:** None\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 2: Frontend Fix Implementation (4-6 hours)\n**Objective:** Implement CSS/styling fixes to resolve all text contrast issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Updated SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx with proper text contrast\n- Fixed badge text colors for dark backgrounds\n- Corrected card text visibility in danger/dark themes\n- Proper table text contrast in all contexts\n- Form control text visibility fixes\n- Comprehensive test suite for contrast verification\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- All text on Improve page clearly readable\n- WCAG 2.1 AA contrast ratios achieved (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large text)\n- Both normal and "Bumpers Off" modes have proper contrast\n- No functionality regression\n- Visual design intent preserved\n- Cross-browser compatibility maintained\n- All automated tests passing\n\n**Dependencies:** Milestone 1 completion\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n- **Low Risk:** This is a focused UI fix with clear scope\n- **Potential Issues:** Bootstrap theme conflicts, responsive design impact\n- **Mitigation:** Thorough testing across devices and browsers\n\n## Success Metrics\n1. **Functional:** All text readable with proper contrast\n2. **Technical:** WCAG 2.1 AA compliance achieved\n3. **Quality:** No regression in existing functionality\n4. **Performance:** No impact on page load or responsiveness\n\n## Project Timeline\n- **Total Duration:** 1-2 days\n- **Milestone 1:** 2-4 hours\n- **Milestone 2:** 4-6 hours\n- **Buffer:** 2-4 hours for testing and refinement'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LuU1h8gz2jRN57DZyBSsZW', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_231219.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_231219.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KgqWfDFzzJao75tAK7G8Xa', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Fix Improve Page UI Readability'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KgqWfDFzzJao75tAK7G8Xa', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018Wq7euk5xRCp8Ff2YBYJe8', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Fix Improve Page UI Readability'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018Wq7euk5xRCp8Ff2YBYJe8', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Designed a targeted remediation architecture focusing on CSS specificity and Bootstrap color class corrections to fix text contrast issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach minimizes risk while ensuring WCAG compliance.", "key_decisions": ["Using targeted CSS fixes rather than major architectural changes to minimize risk and preserve existing functionality", "Leveraging Bootstrap\'s built-in semantic color classes for accessibility compliance instead of custom CSS solutions", "Implementing conditional styling logic that adapts text colors based on background context (normal vs danger mode)", "Focusing solely on the SelfImprovementDashboard component rather than a broader application-wide redesign", "Choosing inline styling and className modifications over CSS Modules or Styled Components to maintain current patterns"], "self_analysis": "I successfully analyzed the UI readability requirements and designed a focused, practical architecture that addresses the contrast issues without over-engineering. The proposal correctly identifies this as a CSS specificity problem rather than requiring new frameworks, and provides specific implementation guidance while considering accessibility standards and risk mitigation."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01YbPJZSFfeUycTCP21Q9tjZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01YbPJZSFfeUycTCP21Q9tjZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: UI Readability Fix for Improve Page\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted remediation architecture** for fixing text readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach focuses on CSS specificity corrections and conditional styling improvements rather than a major architectural redesign.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-level styling fix with cascading CSS improvements\\n**Rationale**: This is a focused bug fix that requires minimal changes to preserve existing functionality while solving the specific contrast problem. A surgical approach ensures no unintended side effects.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n**No new technologies required** - this fix works within the existing stack:\\n\\n### Frontend (Existing)\\n- **React** - Component framework (already in use)\\n- **Bootstrap 5** - CSS framework with built-in color system (leveraging existing theme)\\n- **CSS-in-JS/Inline Styles** - Current styling approach in the component\\n\\n### Why This Approach\\n- **Minimal Risk**: Works with existing technology and patterns\\n- **Fast Implementation**: No new dependencies or learning curve\\n- **Maintainable**: Uses Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes for consistency\\n- **Tested**: Bootstrap\'s color combinations are accessibility-tested\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered:**\\n- CSS Modules: Overkill for a single component fix\\n- Styled Components: Would require major refactoring\\n- New CSS Framework: Unnecessary complexity for a readability fix\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Core Component\\n**SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx**\\n- **Current State**: Contains conditional styling that causes contrast issues\\n- **Responsibility**: Display performance analytics with proper text contrast\\n- **Fix Strategy**: Update styling logic to ensure text colors adapt with background changes\\n\\n### Styling Architecture\\n```\\nSelfImprovementDashboard\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Normal Mode Styling (light backgrounds)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-light, text-dark)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (semantic colors with proper text)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (standard contrast)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 \\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling (dark/danger backgrounds)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-danger, text-white)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (light variants with dark text)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (inverted contrast)\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n```\\nUser Interaction \\u2192 Mode State Change \\u2192 Conditional Styling Logic \\u2192 DOM Update \\u2192 Visual Rendering\\n```\\nNo changes to data flow - only styling application logic.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n**Files to Modify:**\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx  [PRIMARY TARGET]\\n```\\n\\n**Additional Files (if needed):**\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 dashboard-overrides.css  [IF NEEDED - for complex overrides]\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeHelpers.js  [IF NEEDED - for styling logic extraction]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**No database changes required** - this is purely a presentation layer fix.\\n\\n**State Management:**\\n- Existing component state (bumpers mode, performance data) remains unchanged\\n- Only CSS class application logic needs modification\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API changes required** - this fix is entirely frontend styling.\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Process\\n1. **Local Development**: Test fixes in development server\\n2. **Visual Testing**: Verify contrast in both light and dark modes\\n3. **Accessibility Testing**: Use browser dev tools to verify WCAG compliance\\n4. **Cross-Browser Testing**: Ensure fixes work in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n### Deployment\\n- **Type**: Frontend-only deployment\\n- **Risk Level**: Low (isolated component changes)\\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Git revert of specific styling changes\\n- **Testing Required**: Visual regression testing\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\nNo environment-specific configuration needed - styles apply universally.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Manual test cases:\\n1. Load Improve page in normal mode\\n   \\u2192 Verify all text is readable against backgrounds\\n2. Enable \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode  \\n   \\u2192 Verify danger theme maintains text contrast\\n3. Test responsive breakpoints\\n   \\u2192 Ensure readability on mobile/tablet/desktop\\n```\\n\\n### Automated Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Accessibility tests (if jest-axe available):\\ndescribe(\'SelfImprovementDashboard Accessibility\', () => {\\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in normal mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test WCAG compliance\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in bumpers off mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test danger theme compliance\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Browser Testing\\n- **Chrome**: Primary development browser\\n- **Firefox**: Secondary testing\\n- **Safari**: macOS compatibility\\n- **Edge**: Windows compatibility\\n\\n## Specific Technical Implementation\\n\\n### Bootstrap Color Strategy\\n```jsx\\n// Current problematic pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-muted\\">Problem text</span> // This creates dark on dark\\n</Card>\\n\\n// Fixed pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-light\\">Readable text</span>\\n</Card>\\n```\\n\\n### Conditional Styling Logic\\n```jsx\\nconst getTextClass = (isDangerMode, baseClass) => {\\n  if (isDangerMode) {\\n    return baseClass.includes(\'dark\') ? \'text-white\' : \'text-light\';\\n  }\\n  return baseClass.includes(\'light\') ? \'text-dark\' : \'text-white\';\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Option 1: Complete CSS Framework Migration\\n**Rejected**: Too much risk for a simple contrast fix\\n\\n### Option 2: Custom Design System\\n**Rejected**: Overkill - Bootstrap\'s accessibility features solve this when used correctly\\n\\n### Option 3: JavaScript-based Theme Switching\\n**Rejected**: Adds complexity when CSS classes can solve the issue\\n\\n### Option 4: CSS Variables for Dynamic Theming\\n**Considered**: Good for future scalability, but unnecessary for this focused fix\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Breaking Existing Visual Design\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes\\n- Test both modes thoroughly\\n- Take screenshots for before/after comparison\\n\\n### Risk 2: CSS Specificity Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use inline styles for high specificity when needed\\n- Follow existing patterns in the codebase\\n- Test in actual browser environment\\n\\n### Risk 3: Performance Impact\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- No new CSS files or frameworks\\n- Minimal additional class computations\\n- No impact on bundle size\\n\\n### Risk 4: Cross-Browser Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use standard Bootstrap classes (well-tested across browsers)\\n- Test in multiple browsers\\n- Avoid custom CSS properties that might not be supported\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Design Questions for User Review\\n1. **Color Preference**: Should danger mode use red backgrounds with white text, or prefer orange/yellow for better accessibility?\\n2. **Badge Styling**: For dark badges, prefer white text or switch to light-colored badges with dark text?\\n3. **Table Styling**: In dark mode, prefer inverted table colors or maintain current table style with better text contrast?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input\\n1. **Approach**: Pure inline styling vs. conditional CSS classes?\\n2. **Scope**: Fix only the reported component or audit entire application for similar issues?\\n3. **Testing**: Include automated accessibility tests or rely on manual verification?\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Immediate Fix (1-2 hours)\\n- Identify and fix the most critical contrast issues\\n- Focus on badges and card text\\n- Test both normal and danger modes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Comprehensive Audit (2-3 hours)\\n- Review all text elements in the component\\n- Ensure WCAG compliance\\n- Add consistent styling patterns\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing and Validation (1 hour)\\n- Cross-browser testing\\n- Accessibility validation\\n- User acceptance testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Contrast Ratio**: All text meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large)\\n2. **Visual Verification**: User confirms readability issues are resolved\\n3. **No Regression**: All existing functionality works unchanged\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable impact on page load or rendering performance\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **User Approval**: Confirm this architectural approach before implementation\\n2. **Development**: Implement the CSS fixes following this plan\\n3. **Testing**: Execute the testing strategy outlined above\\n4. **Deployment**: Deploy with the low-risk strategy described\\n\\nThis architecture provides a focused, low-risk solution that addresses the specific readability problem while maintaining system stability and existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BUHY1h5vfUNTdFM3tgDJ1Q', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Frontend Fix Implementation - Implement CSS/styling fixes to resolve all text contrast issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BUHY1h5vfUNTdFM3tgDJ1Q', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 7, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md", "dependencies": ["Task 2 (Card Text Contrast) \\u2192 Task 3 (Table Text)", "Task 2 (Card Text Contrast) \\u2192 Task 4 (Form Controls)", "Tasks 1-4 \\u2192 Task 5 (Conditional Logic)", "Task 5 \\u2192 Task 6 (Cross-Browser Testing)", "Task 6 \\u2192 Task 7 (Performance Testing)"], "message": "Frontend task breakdown completed for CSS/styling fixes to resolve text contrast issues in SelfImprovementDashboard component. Identified 7 specific tasks organized in 3 phases: component-level fixes (badges, cards, tables, forms), system-level integration (conditional styling logic), and validation/QA (cross-browser and performance testing). All tasks focus on achieving WCAG 2.1 AA compliance while preserving existing functionality and design."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KtnEb9VWRDoGxnbDiwhA3i', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/test_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Frontend Fix Implementation - Implement CSS/styling fixes to resolve all text contrast issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m2.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KtnEb9VWRDoGxnbDiwhA3i', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "test_tasks_