{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:22:53", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-4ca16fd9-51ec-4615-8266-88d4ec385f0d', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Foundation Infrastructure - Establish core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security including frequent coherent commits, branch-based development, state persistence & recovery, and secrets management",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016vjiubSohyoyDCK459YooG', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016vjiubSohyoyDCK459YooG', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: UI Readability Fix for Improve Page\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted remediation architecture** for fixing text readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach focuses on CSS specificity corrections and conditional styling improvements rather than a major architectural redesign.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-level styling fix with cascading CSS improvements\\n**Rationale**: This is a focused bug fix that requires minimal changes to preserve existing functionality while solving the specific contrast problem. A surgical approach ensures no unintended side effects.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n**No new technologies required** - this fix works within the existing stack:\\n\\n### Frontend (Existing)\\n- **React** - Component framework (already in use)\\n- **Bootstrap 5** - CSS framework with built-in color system (leveraging existing theme)\\n- **CSS-in-JS/Inline Styles** - Current styling approach in the component\\n\\n### Why This Approach\\n- **Minimal Risk**: Works with existing technology and patterns\\n- **Fast Implementation**: No new dependencies or learning curve\\n- **Maintainable**: Uses Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes for consistency\\n- **Tested**: Bootstrap\'s color combinations are accessibility-tested\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered:**\\n- CSS Modules: Overkill for a single component fix\\n- Styled Components: Would require major refactoring\\n- New CSS Framework: Unnecessary complexity for a readability fix\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Core Component\\n**SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx**\\n- **Current State**: Contains conditional styling that causes contrast issues\\n- **Responsibility**: Display performance analytics with proper text contrast\\n- **Fix Strategy**: Update styling logic to ensure text colors adapt with background changes\\n\\n### Styling Architecture\\n```\\nSelfImprovementDashboard\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Normal Mode Styling (light backgrounds)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-light, text-dark)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (semantic colors with proper text)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (standard contrast)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 \\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling (dark/danger backgrounds)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-danger, text-white)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (light variants with dark text)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (inverted contrast)\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n```\\nUser Interaction \\u2192 Mode State Change \\u2192 Conditional Styling Logic \\u2192 DOM Update \\u2192 Visual Rendering\\n```\\nNo changes to data flow - only styling application logic.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n**Files to Modify:**\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx  [PRIMARY TARGET]\\n```\\n\\n**Additional Files (if needed):**\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 dashboard-overrides.css  [IF NEEDED - for complex overrides]\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeHelpers.js  [IF NEEDED - for styling logic extraction]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**No database changes required** - this is purely a presentation layer fix.\\n\\n**State Management:**\\n- Existing component state (bumpers mode, performance data) remains unchanged\\n- Only CSS class application logic needs modification\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API changes required** - this fix is entirely frontend styling.\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Process\\n1. **Local Development**: Test fixes in development server\\n2. **Visual Testing**: Verify contrast in both light and dark modes\\n3. **Accessibility Testing**: Use browser dev tools to verify WCAG compliance\\n4. **Cross-Browser Testing**: Ensure fixes work in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n### Deployment\\n- **Type**: Frontend-only deployment\\n- **Risk Level**: Low (isolated component changes)\\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Git revert of specific styling changes\\n- **Testing Required**: Visual regression testing\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\nNo environment-specific configuration needed - styles apply universally.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Manual test cases:\\n1. Load Improve page in normal mode\\n   \\u2192 Verify all text is readable against backgrounds\\n2. Enable \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode  \\n   \\u2192 Verify danger theme maintains text contrast\\n3. Test responsive breakpoints\\n   \\u2192 Ensure readability on mobile/tablet/desktop\\n```\\n\\n### Automated Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Accessibility tests (if jest-axe available):\\ndescribe(\'SelfImprovementDashboard Accessibility\', () => {\\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in normal mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test WCAG compliance\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in bumpers off mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test danger theme compliance\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Browser Testing\\n- **Chrome**: Primary development browser\\n- **Firefox**: Secondary testing\\n- **Safari**: macOS compatibility\\n- **Edge**: Windows compatibility\\n\\n## Specific Technical Implementation\\n\\n### Bootstrap Color Strategy\\n```jsx\\n// Current problematic pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-muted\\">Problem text</span> // This creates dark on dark\\n</Card>\\n\\n// Fixed pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-light\\">Readable text</span>\\n</Card>\\n```\\n\\n### Conditional Styling Logic\\n```jsx\\nconst getTextClass = (isDangerMode, baseClass) => {\\n  if (isDangerMode) {\\n    return baseClass.includes(\'dark\') ? \'text-white\' : \'text-light\';\\n  }\\n  return baseClass.includes(\'light\') ? \'text-dark\' : \'text-white\';\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Option 1: Complete CSS Framework Migration\\n**Rejected**: Too much risk for a simple contrast fix\\n\\n### Option 2: Custom Design System\\n**Rejected**: Overkill - Bootstrap\'s accessibility features solve this when used correctly\\n\\n### Option 3: JavaScript-based Theme Switching\\n**Rejected**: Adds complexity when CSS classes can solve the issue\\n\\n### Option 4: CSS Variables for Dynamic Theming\\n**Considered**: Good for future scalability, but unnecessary for this focused fix\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Breaking Existing Visual Design\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes\\n- Test both modes thoroughly\\n- Take screenshots for before/after comparison\\n\\n### Risk 2: CSS Specificity Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use inline styles for high specificity when needed\\n- Follow existing patterns in the codebase\\n- Test in actual browser environment\\n\\n### Risk 3: Performance Impact\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- No new CSS files or frameworks\\n- Minimal additional class computations\\n- No impact on bundle size\\n\\n### Risk 4: Cross-Browser Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use standard Bootstrap classes (well-tested across browsers)\\n- Test in multiple browsers\\n- Avoid custom CSS properties that might not be supported\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Design Questions for User Review\\n1. **Color Preference**: Should danger mode use red backgrounds with white text, or prefer orange/yellow for better accessibility?\\n2. **Badge Styling**: For dark badges, prefer white text or switch to light-colored badges with dark text?\\n3. **Table Styling**: In dark mode, prefer inverted table colors or maintain current table style with better text contrast?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input\\n1. **Approach**: Pure inline styling vs. conditional CSS classes?\\n2. **Scope**: Fix only the reported component or audit entire application for similar issues?\\n3. **Testing**: Include automated accessibility tests or rely on manual verification?\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Immediate Fix (1-2 hours)\\n- Identify and fix the most critical contrast issues\\n- Focus on badges and card text\\n- Test both normal and danger modes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Comprehensive Audit (2-3 hours)\\n- Review all text elements in the component\\n- Ensure WCAG compliance\\n- Add consistent styling patterns\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing and Validation (1 hour)\\n- Cross-browser testing\\n- Accessibility validation\\n- User acceptance testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Contrast Ratio**: All text meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large)\\n2. **Visual Verification**: User confirms readability issues are resolved\\n3. **No Regression**: All existing functionality works unchanged\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable impact on page load or rendering performance\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **User Approval**: Confirm this architectural approach before implementation\\n2. **Development**: Implement the CSS fixes following this plan\\n3. **Testing**: Execute the testing strategy outlined above\\n4. **Deployment**: Deploy with the low-risk strategy described\\n\\nThis architecture provides a focused, low-risk solution that addresses the specific readability problem while maintaining system stability and existing functionality."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019g58ihrTidf6XXAW2LBovj', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019g58ihrTidf6XXAW2LBovj', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Future Features Implementation Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nImplement all 22 features and enhancements defined in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/current/FUTURE_FEATURES.md` to create a comprehensive, production-ready multi-agent development platform with advanced workflow capabilities, quality assurance, cost management, and user experience improvements.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Development Workflow**: Implement branch-based development, frequent commits, concurrent agent sessions, and agent collaboration protocols\\n2. **Code Quality**: Add automated code review, continuous integration, and documentation generation agents\\n3. **Cost & Performance**: Implement cost tracking, performance metrics dashboard, and agent performance learning\\n4. **User Experience**: Create interactive web dashboard and integration capabilities\\n5. **Advanced Features**: Develop knowledge repository agent, self-healing capabilities, and multi-provider LLM routing\\n6. **Infrastructure**: Add state persistence, secrets management, and audit trail capabilities\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### HIGH PRIORITY Features (Immediate Implementation)\\n1. **Frequent Coherent Commits** - Auto-commit tool with proper formatting and agent attribution\\n2. **Branch-Based Development System** - Git workflow with milestone branches and PR management\\n3. **Continuous Integration Agent** - Automated testing, linting, and quality checks\\n4. **Cost Tracking & Budgeting** - API cost monitoring with alerts and reporting\\n5. **Knowledge Repository Agent** - Centralized project context and architectural decision tracking\\n6. **State Persistence & Recovery** - Checkpoint system for pipeline recovery\\n7. **Secrets Management** - Secure API key and credential handling\\n\\n### MEDIUM PRIORITY Features (Phase 2)\\n8. **Concurrent Agent Sessions** - Parallel execution on different branches\\n9. **Agent Collaboration Protocol** - Cross-branch communication and event system\\n10. **Automated Code Review Agent** - Pre-commit code quality analysis\\n11. **Performance Metrics Dashboard** - Agent success rates and efficiency tracking\\n12. **Interactive Web Dashboard** - Live execution visualization with manual intervention\\n13. **Multi-Provider LLM Routing** - Task-based model selection optimization\\n14. **Audit Trail** - Comprehensive logging of all agent actions\\n\\n### ADVANCED Features (Phase 3)\\n15. **Agent Performance Learning** - Self-optimizing task assignment based on historical data\\n16. **Self-Healing Agents** - Automatic failure detection and strategy adjustment\\n17. **Agent Composition Engine** - Automatic pipeline generation based on task requirements\\n18. **Docker-Based Agent Execution** - Containerized agent environments\\n\\n### FUTURE Features (Phase 4)\\n19. **Documentation Generator Agent** - Automated documentation and changelog generation\\n20. **Slack/Discord Integration** - Team communication and command interface\\n21. **Distributed Agent Execution** - Multi-machine agent coordination\\n22. **Voice Interface** - Natural language interaction with the ensemble system\\n\\n## Target Users\\n- Development teams using the Ensemble system for automated development\\n- Project managers needing visibility into agent activities and costs\\n- System administrators managing multi-agent infrastructure\\n- Individual developers leveraging AI assistance for complex projects\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **All HIGH PRIORITY features** (7 features) fully implemented and tested\\n2. **Branch-based workflow** successfully managing parallel agent execution\\n3. **Cost tracking system** providing accurate usage monitoring and budget alerts\\n4. **Knowledge repository** maintaining comprehensive project context\\n5. **CI/CD pipeline** automatically validating all agent-generated code\\n6. **State persistence** enabling reliable recovery from interruptions\\n7. **Zero regressions** in existing functionality\\n8. **Complete test coverage** for all new features\\n9. **Performance benchmarks** showing improved efficiency over current system\\n10. **User documentation** for all implemented features\\n\\n## Constraints\\n1. **Maintain backward compatibility** with existing agent implementations\\n2. **Follow existing code patterns** and architectural conventions in the Ensemble system\\n3. **Incremental delivery** - implement in logical milestones, not monolithic changes\\n4. **Resource efficiency** - new features should not significantly increase baseline costs\\n5. **Security first** - all credential and secret management must follow security best practices\\n6. **Testing requirements** - all features must include comprehensive test coverage\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n1. **Git Integration**: Enhanced git_commit, git_branch, git_merge tools with proper conflict resolution\\n2. **Database Integration**: Persistent storage for cost tracking, performance metrics, and knowledge base\\n3. **API Enhancement**: Extended agent toolkit with new collaboration and monitoring tools\\n4. **Security Framework**: Vault integration for secrets management with audit capabilities\\n5. **Monitoring Infrastructure**: Performance metrics collection and alerting system\\n6. **Recovery Mechanisms**: Checkpoint and rollback capabilities for long-running operations\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Voice interface implementation (marked as FUTURE)\\n- Complete distributed execution across multiple machines\\n- Integration with external project management tools beyond Slack/Discord\\n- Mobile application interface\\n- Real-time collaborative editing features\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Milestones 0-1)\\n- Frequent commits system\\n- Branch-based development\\n- State persistence\\n- Secrets management\\n\\n### Phase 2: Quality & Visibility (Milestones 2-3) \\n- CI/CD agent\\n- Cost tracking\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Code review automation\\n\\n### Phase 3: Advanced Intelligence (Milestones 4-5)\\n- Knowledge repository agent\\n- Agent performance learning\\n- Multi-provider routing\\n- Self-healing capabilities\\n\\n### Phase 4: User Experience (Milestones 6+)\\n- Web dashboard\\n- Integration capabilities\\n- Advanced collaboration features\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Current git tooling is functional** - building on existing git integration\\n2. **Database support exists** - using existing data persistence patterns\\n3. **Agent communication protocols** can be enhanced without breaking existing agents\\n4. **Performance monitoring infrastructure** can be added without significant overhead\\n5. **User approval process** exists for branch merging and deployment decisions\\n6. **API cost tracking** can be implemented without modifying core LLM integration\\n7. **Security requirements** align with standard enterprise practices\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- Existing Ensemble agent architecture and runtime system\\n- Git repository structure and branch management capabilities\\n- Database/persistence layer for metrics and state storage\\n- LLM provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) for cost tracking integration\\n- Web framework support for dashboard implementation\\n- Container infrastructure for advanced execution features\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n1. **Complex git workflows** - implement with comprehensive testing and rollback capabilities\\n2. **Agent coordination conflicts** - design robust locking and conflict resolution mechanisms  \\n3. **Performance impact** - implement monitoring and resource limits for new features\\n4. **Security vulnerabilities** - conduct security review of all credential handling\\n5. **Integration complexity** - phase implementation to validate each component independently\\n6. **Cost overruns** - implement budget controls and usage alerts from day one"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013dGUo9GLN6HY3AKxfKzany', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Foundation Infrastructure Milestone\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone establishes core infrastructure for enhanced git workflows, state management, and security. Testing focuses on validating the reliability, security, and robustness of fundamental systems that all future features will depend on.\n\n## Test Coverage Goals\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 85% for business logic components\n- **Integration Coverage**: 100% of all git operations, state persistence, and security functions\n- **E2E Coverage**: Critical workflows for commit automation, branch management, and recovery scenarios\n\n## Testing Framework Stack\n- **Backend**: pytest with mocks for external dependencies\n- **Frontend**: Jest + React Testing Library\n- **E2E**: Playwright for git workflow automation\n- **Security**: Custom security tests for secrets management\n- **Performance**: Load tests for state persistence under concurrent access\n\n## Core Components to Test\n\n### 1. Enhanced Git Operations\n**Components**:\n- `git_commit` enhanced tool with auto-formatting\n- `git_branch` tool with milestone branch patterns\n- `git_merge` tool with conflict resolution\n- Commit message generation with agent attribution\n\n**Critical Business Logic**:\n- Commit message formatting and agent attribution\n- Branch naming conventions and validation\n- Merge conflict detection and resolution strategies\n- Git state validation before operations\n\n### 2. State Persistence & Recovery System\n**Components**:\n- Checkpoint creation and restoration\n- Pipeline state serialization\n- Recovery mechanism for interrupted operations\n- State validation and integrity checks\n\n**Critical Business Logic**:\n- State consistency across agent restarts\n- Recovery point identification and rollback\n- Concurrent access handling\n- Data integrity validation\n\n### 3. Secrets Management\n**Components**:\n- API key secure storage and retrieval\n- Credential encryption/decryption\n- Access control and audit logging\n- Integration with external secret stores\n\n**Critical Business Logic**:\n- Encryption key management\n- Access permission validation\n- Secure credential rotation\n- Audit trail generation\n\n## Test Task Breakdown\n\n### Unit Tests (22 tasks)\n\n#### Enhanced Git Operations (8 tasks)\n**TASK-U001**: Test commit message generation with agent attribution\n- Test agent metadata inclusion in commit messages\n- Validate commit message formatting standards\n- Mock git repository operations\n\n**TASK-U002**: Test branch name validation and formatting  \n- Test milestone-based branch naming conventions\n- Validate branch name sanitization\n- Test invalid branch name rejection\n\n**TASK-U003**: Test git operation state validation\n- Test pre-commit validation checks\n- Test repository state assessment\n- Mock git status operations\n\n**TASK-U004**: Test merge conflict detection logic\n- Test conflict identification algorithms\n- Test merge strategy selection\n- Mock git merge scenarios\n\n**TASK-U005**: Test commit atomicity and rollback\n- Test partial commit failure handling\n- Test rollback mechanisms\n- Mock git operation failures\n\n**TASK-U006**: Test branch creation with proper base selection\n- Test base branch identification logic\n- Test branch creation validation\n- Mock branch hierarchy operations\n\n**TASK-U007**: Test git history analysis for auto-commit decisions\n- Test commit frequency analysis\n- Test change magnitude assessment\n- Mock git log parsing\n\n**TASK-U008**: Test git operation permission validation\n- Test repository access permissions\n- Test operation authorization checks\n- Mock permission denial scenarios\n\n#### State Persistence (8 tasks)\n**TASK-U009**: Test checkpoint creation and serialization\n- Test agent state serialization\n- Test checkpoint data structure validation\n- Mock file system operations\n\n**TASK-U010**: Test checkpoint restoration and deserialization\n- Test state restoration accuracy\n- Test data integrity validation\n- Mock corrupted checkpoint handling\n\n**TASK-U011**: Test concurrent checkpoint access\n- Test multi-agent checkpoint coordination\n- Test lock mechanism functionality\n- Mock concurrent access scenarios\n\n**TASK-U012**: Test state validation and integrity checks\n- Test checksum validation\n- Test state consistency verification\n- Mock integrity failure scenarios\n\n**TASK-U013**: Test recovery point identification\n- Test recovery point selection logic\n- Test partial recovery scenarios\n- Mock incomplete checkpoint data\n\n**TASK-U014**: Test pipeline state tracking\n- Test agent progress tracking\n- Test milestone completion detection\n- Mock agent state transitions\n\n**TASK-U015**: Test cleanup and retention policies\n- Test old checkpoint removal\n- Test storage space management\n- Mock storage limit scenarios\n\n**TASK-U016**: Test cross-agent state sharing\n- Test shared state synchronization\n- Test state conflict resolution\n- Mock state merge scenarios\n\n#### Secrets Management (6 tasks)\n**TASK-U017**: Test credential encryption/decryption\n- Test encryption algorithm implementation\n- Test key derivation functions\n- Mock encryption key operations\n\n**TASK-U018**: Test access control validation\n- Test permission-based access controls\n- Test role-based authorization\n- Mock unauthorized access attempts\n\n**TASK-U019**: Test secure storage operations\n- Test credential storage mechanisms\n- Test storage encryption validation\n- Mock storage failure scenarios\n\n**TASK-U020**: Test credential rotation logic\n- Test automatic credential updates\n- Test rotation scheduling\n- Mock credential provider APIs\n\n**TASK-U021**: Test audit logging functionality\n- Test access event logging\n- Test audit trail generation\n- Mock logging system failures\n\n**TASK-U022**: Test secrets validation and health checks\n- Test credential validity verification\n- Test expired credential detection\n- Mock credential validation APIs\n\n### Integration Tests (15 tasks)\n\n#### Git Workflow Integration (6 tasks)\n**TASK-I001**: Test complete commit automation workflow\n- Test end-to-end auto-commit process\n- Integrate with real git repository\n- Validate commit appears in git history\n\n**TASK-I002**: Test branch-based development workflow\n- Test milestone branch creation to merge cycle\n- Integrate with git repository structure\n- Validate branch protection and merge requirements\n\n**TASK-I003**: Test merge conflict resolution integration\n- Test conflict detection with real git scenarios\n- Integrate conflict resolution with merge tools\n- Validate successful merge completion\n\n**TASK-I004**: Test git operation error handling and recovery\n- Test git command failure scenarios\n- Integrate with error reporting systems\n- Validate graceful failure recovery\n\n**TASK-I005**: Test concurrent git operations coordination\n- Test multiple agents performing git operations\n- Integrate with locking mechanisms\n- Validate operation serialization\n\n**TASK-I006**: Test git history integration with state tracking\n- Test commit history correlation with agent states\n- Integrate git metadata with checkpoint system\n- Validate historical state reconstruction\n\n#### State System Integration (5 tasks)\n**TASK-I007**: Test state persistence with file system\n- Test checkpoint file creation and retrieval\n- Integrate with actual file system storage\n- Validate data persistence across restarts\n\n**TASK-I008**: Test recovery system integration\n- Test complete pipeline recovery from checkpoints\n- Integrate with agent restart mechanisms\n- Validate state consistency after recovery\n\n**TASK-I009**: Test state sharing between agents\n- Test inter-agent state communication\n- Integrate with message passing systems\n- Validate state synchronization accuracy\n\n**TASK-I010**: Test state cleanup with storage systems\n- Test automated cleanup processes\n- Integrate with file system monitoring\n- Validate storage space management\n\n**TASK-I011**: Test state validation with data integrity\n- Test comprehensive state validation\n- Integrate with data validation libraries\n- Validate error detection and reporting\n\n#### Security Integration (4 tasks)\n**TASK-I012**: Test secrets management with external providers\n- Test integration with HashiCorp Vault or similar\n- Integrate with API key management services\n- Validate secure credential retrieval\n\n**TASK-I013**: Test encrypted storage integration\n- Test credential encryption with storage systems\n- Integrate with encryption libraries\n- Validate data protection at rest\n\n**TASK-I014**: Test audit logging integration\n- Test audit log generation and storage\n- Integrate with logging infrastructure\n- Validate audit trail completeness\n\n**TASK-I015**: Test security validation with authentication\n- Test credential-based authentication flows\n- Integrate with identity management systems\n- Validate access control enforcement\n\n### End-to-End Tests (8 tasks)\n\n#### Critical User Journeys (8 tasks)\n**TASK-E001**: Test complete milestone development workflow\n- User creates milestone with multiple features\n- Agents create branches, make commits, handle merges\n- Validate entire workflow from start to delivery\n\n**TASK-E002**: Test pipeline failure and recovery scenario\n- Simulate agent failure during development\n- Test recovery from latest checkpoint\n- Validate continuation without data loss\n\n**TASK-E003**: Test concurrent agent development workflow\n- Multiple agents working on different features\n- Test branch management and merge coordination\n- Validate no conflicts or lost work\n\n**TASK-E004**: Test secrets rotation during active development\n- API credentials expire during agent execution\n- Test automatic credential refresh\n- Validate uninterrupted agent operation\n\n**TASK-E005**: Test git conflict resolution workflow\n- Agents create conflicting changes\n- Test automatic conflict detection and resolution\n- Validate successful merge completion\n\n**TASK-E006**: Test state corruption recovery\n- Simulate checkpoint corruption\n- Test fallback to previous valid state\n- Validate minimal work loss\n\n**TASK-E007**: Test long-running development session\n- Extended multi-agent development session\n- Test checkpoint frequency and storage efficiency\n- Validate system stability over time\n\n**TASK-E008**: Test security breach simulation\n- Simulate unauthorized access attempt\n- Test security controls and audit logging\n- Validate system protection and alerting\n\n## Test Data Requirements\n\n### Git Repository Test Data\n- Clean test repositories for each test scenario\n- Pre-configured branch structures for workflow testing\n- Sample commit histories for conflict simulation\n- Invalid repository states for error testing\n\n### State Persistence Test Data\n- Valid checkpoint files for restoration testing\n- Corrupted checkpoint data for error handling\n- Large state objects for performance testing\n- Concurrent access scenarios for race condition testing\n\n### Secrets Management Test Data\n- Test API keys and credentials (non-functional)\n- Encrypted credential samples\n- Access control configuration data\n- Audit log sample data\n\n### Performance Test Data\n- Large numbers of concurrent operations\n- Extensive git histories for performance benchmarking\n- Multiple checkpoint files for cleanup testing\n- High-frequency state updates for stress testing\n\n## Mock Strategy\n\n### External Dependencies to Mock\n- **Git Commands**: Mock all `git` CLI operations for unit tests\n- **File System**: Mock file operations for isolated testing\n- **External APIs**: Mock credential provider APIs\n- **Network Operations**: Mock all external network calls\n- **System Resources**: Mock system-level resource checks\n\n### Real Integration Points\n- **Actual Git Repositories**: Use real git repos for integration tests\n- **File System Storage**: Use real file storage for integration tests\n- **Encryption Libraries**: Use real crypto libraries for security tests\n- **Database Connections**: Use real database for state persistence tests\n\n## Performance Benchmarks\n\n### Git Operations Performance\n- **Commit Creation**: < 2 seconds for standard commits\n- **Branch Operations**: < 1 second for branch creation/switching\n- **Merge Operations**: < 5 seconds for standard merges\n- **History Analysis**: < 3 seconds for 1000 commit analysis\n\n### State Persistence Performance\n- **Checkpoint Creation**: < 1 second for typical agent state\n- **State Restoration**: < 2 seconds for complete recovery\n- **Concurrent Access**: Handle 10 concurrent agents\n- **Storage Efficiency**: < 10MB per checkpoint\n\n### Security Operations Performance\n- **Credential Retrieval**: < 500ms for encrypted credential access\n- **Access Validation**: < 100ms for permission checks\n- **Audit Logging**: < 50ms for audit event recording\n- **Encryption/Decryption**: < 200ms for typical credential sizes\n\n## Test Environment Requirements\n\n### Development Environment\n- Git repository with test branches\n- Local file system for state storage\n- Mock credential providers\n- Test databases for integration\n\n### CI/CD Environment  \n- Automated test git repositories\n- Containerized test environments\n- Secure credential storage for integration tests\n- Performance monitoring tools\n\n### Security Testing Environment\n- Isolated network environment\n- Security scanning tools\n- Audit log analysis tools\n- Penetration testing capabilities\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Unit Test Success\n- 85% code coverage achieved\n- All business logic functions tested\n- Edge cases and error conditions covered\n- Fast test execution (< 30 seconds total)\n\n### Integration Test Success\n- All external integrations verified\n- Real-world scenarios successfully tested\n- Error handling validated with actual systems\n- Performance benchmarks met\n\n### E2E Test Success\n- Complete user workflows validated\n- Recovery scenarios successfully tested\n- Security controls verified\n- System stability demonstrated\n\n### Overall Success\n- Zero critical bugs in foundation infrastructure\n- All performance benchmarks exceeded\n- Security audit requirements satisfied\n- Ready for Phase 2 feature development\n\n## Risk Mitigation Testing\n\n### High-Risk Areas\n1. **Git Operation Conflicts**: Extensive testing of concurrent git operations\n2. **State Corruption**: Comprehensive testing of recovery mechanisms\n3. **Security Vulnerabilities**: Thorough security testing and penetration testing\n4. **Performance Degradation**: Load testing and performance monitoring\n5. **Integration Failures**: Extensive testing of external system integrations\n\n### Contingency Testing\n- Backup system validation\n- Rollback procedure testing\n- Disaster recovery scenario testing\n- Performance degradation response testing\n\nThis comprehensive test strategy ensures the foundation infrastructure is robust, secure, and performant enough to support all future milestone development.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013dGUo9GLN6HY3AKxfKzany', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260114_232252.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260114_232252.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
