{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:24:11", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8e7ceef5-1581-4137-8763-9381bbde6df6', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Recovery Agent System"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011t4vJ84Dw2WjVh4c7T5edZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Gy5tX8D3dfuLQ4jSvJtPmD', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011t4vJ84Dw2WjVh4c7T5edZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Recovery Agent System Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy pane rather than keeping them isolated in the recovery dashboard.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when jobs are recovered through the recovery system:\\n1. Jobs run in a separate recovery context via `RecoveryOrchestrator._retry_agent()`\\n2. Recovered jobs are not visible in the main Agent Hierarchy tree on the Activity view\\n3. The recovery pane shows job status, but jobs may run to completion without appearing in the main UI\\n4. Users cannot track recovered jobs with the same visibility as regular jobs\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a `recovery_agent.md` agent definition in the `leadership/` directory\\n2. Modify the recovery orchestration to spawn Executive Directors via this Recovery Agent for each recovered job\\n3. Ensure recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs\\n4. Maintain visibility into recovery status while integrating with the main workflow\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n- Create a new agent type `leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- The Recovery Agent should:\\n  - Accept recovery task information (failed agent details, failure reason, recovery strategy)\\n  - Spawn an Executive Director to manage the recovered task\\n  - Pass the original user_vision/task to the Executive Director\\n  - Track recovery attempts and escalation history\\n\\n### FR2: Recovery Agent Capabilities\\n- **Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\\n- **Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers or coordinators (must go through Executive Director)\\n- **Input**: Recovery task details from the recovery queue\\n- **Output**: Status of recovery attempt, spawned Executive Director ID\\n\\n### FR3: Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Modify `swarm_recovery.py` to:\\n  - Use spawn_agent tool to spawn Recovery Agent instead of directly calling `_retry_agent`\\n  - Pass necessary context: original input_data, failure reason, recovery strategy\\n  - The Recovery Agent then spawns Executive Director with proper swarm state registration\\n\\n### FR4: Swarm State Integration\\n- Recovered jobs must:\\n  - Register in swarm_state as new agents with proper parent relationships\\n  - Appear in the `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint response\\n  - Be visible in the AgentHierarchyTree component\\n  - Link back to the original failed job via metadata\\n\\n### FR5: UI Visibility\\n- No UI changes required (feature request is backend-focused)\\n- Existing AgentHierarchyTree will automatically show recovered jobs once they\'re in swarm_state\\n- Recovery Dashboard can continue to show recovery-specific status info\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR1: Backward Compatibility\\n- Existing recovery dashboard should continue to work\\n- Recovery queue and history should still be populated\\n\\n### NFR2: Traceability\\n- Each recovery attempt should maintain reference to:\\n  - Original failed agent_id\\n  - Recovery queue entry\\n  - Failure reason and strategy applied\\n\\n## Technical Design Notes\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n    \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - ID of the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"original_session_id\\": \\"string - Session that contained the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"agent_type\\": \\"string - Type of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"agent_name\\": \\"string - Name of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"input_data\\": \\"object - Original input to the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"string - Why the agent failed/stalled\\",\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": \\"integer - Which recovery attempt this is\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"output_directory\\": \\"string - Where to write artifacts\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"recovery_id\\": \\"string - ID of this recovery attempt\\",\\n  \\"spawned_executive_id\\": \\"string - ID of the Executive Director spawned\\",\\n  \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - Reference to original failed agent\\",\\n  \\"message\\": \\"string - Status message\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"string - Performance analysis\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The Recovery Agent will be spawned by the RecoveryOrchestrator (which will need access to spawn_agent)\\n- The Executive Director spawned for recovery will create a new session or join existing session\\n- Recovery tasks will be visible both in recovery dashboard AND agent hierarchy\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\\n2. Users can track recovery progress the same way they track regular job progress\\n3. Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\\n4. No regression in existing recovery functionality\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Gy5tX8D3dfuLQ4jSvJtPmD', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/brass-band-achievements", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/css_accessibility_analysis_report.md", "tests/runtime/agents/test_brass_band_achievements.py"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "56 seconds ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "56 seconds ago"}, {"hash": "a81afe1939da863370999b4c3bff0b885cdea04a", "message": "Executive Director: Complete UI readability fix project for Improve page", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "dbb4e5cdf62e28d6aa04d1d80ad96ffa174e4b4c", "message": "Complete milestone 2: UI readability fix implementation and testing", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "91abbd5a22e7ab7748eb34750e92010366b3de1f", "message": "Complete milestone 1: UI readability analysis and architecture planning", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "85 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "92d30084e33cc181990ccee0a29990edf61fe10b", "message": "Implement whimsicalNames utility module with arrays, hash function, name generation, and emoji mapping", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "86 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-5-20251101', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 91.2%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.0\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties':