{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:24:39", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2937b67d-cb2a-4c3a-a77e-01dc8d27ef0a', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Recovery Agent System"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01L5VUyP4eAVdkc1Eid4vDSH', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BjTJ5DKrRGyB9BSxGB4xEN', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01L5VUyP4eAVdkc1Eid4vDSH', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Recovery Agent System Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy pane rather than keeping them isolated in the recovery dashboard.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when jobs are recovered through the recovery system:\\n1. Jobs run in a separate recovery context via `RecoveryOrchestrator._retry_agent()`\\n2. Recovered jobs are not visible in the main Agent Hierarchy tree on the Activity view\\n3. The recovery pane shows job status, but jobs may run to completion without appearing in the main UI\\n4. Users cannot track recovered jobs with the same visibility as regular jobs\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a `recovery_agent.md` agent definition in the `leadership/` directory\\n2. Modify the recovery orchestration to spawn Executive Directors via this Recovery Agent for each recovered job\\n3. Ensure recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs\\n4. Maintain visibility into recovery status while integrating with the main workflow\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n- Create a new agent type `leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- The Recovery Agent should:\\n  - Accept recovery task information (failed agent details, failure reason, recovery strategy)\\n  - Spawn an Executive Director to manage the recovered task\\n  - Pass the original user_vision/task to the Executive Director\\n  - Track recovery attempts and escalation history\\n\\n### FR2: Recovery Agent Capabilities\\n- **Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\\n- **Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers or coordinators (must go through Executive Director)\\n- **Input**: Recovery task details from the recovery queue\\n- **Output**: Status of recovery attempt, spawned Executive Director ID\\n\\n### FR3: Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Modify `swarm_recovery.py` to:\\n  - Use spawn_agent tool to spawn Recovery Agent instead of directly calling `_retry_agent`\\n  - Pass necessary context: original input_data, failure reason, recovery strategy\\n  - The Recovery Agent then spawns Executive Director with proper swarm state registration\\n\\n### FR4: Swarm State Integration\\n- Recovered jobs must:\\n  - Register in swarm_state as new agents with proper parent relationships\\n  - Appear in the `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint response\\n  - Be visible in the AgentHierarchyTree component\\n  - Link back to the original failed job via metadata\\n\\n### FR5: UI Visibility\\n- No UI changes required (feature request is backend-focused)\\n- Existing AgentHierarchyTree will automatically show recovered jobs once they\'re in swarm_state\\n- Recovery Dashboard can continue to show recovery-specific status info\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR1: Backward Compatibility\\n- Existing recovery dashboard should continue to work\\n- Recovery queue and history should still be populated\\n\\n### NFR2: Traceability\\n- Each recovery attempt should maintain reference to:\\n  - Original failed agent_id\\n  - Recovery queue entry\\n  - Failure reason and strategy applied\\n\\n## Technical Design Notes\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n    \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - ID of the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"original_session_id\\": \\"string - Session that contained the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"agent_type\\": \\"string - Type of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"agent_name\\": \\"string - Name of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"input_data\\": \\"object - Original input to the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"string - Why the agent failed/stalled\\",\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": \\"integer - Which recovery attempt this is\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"output_directory\\": \\"string - Where to write artifacts\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"recovery_id\\": \\"string - ID of this recovery attempt\\",\\n  \\"spawned_executive_id\\": \\"string - ID of the Executive Director spawned\\",\\n  \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - Reference to original failed agent\\",\\n  \\"message\\": \\"string - Status message\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"string - Performance analysis\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The Recovery Agent will be spawned by the RecoveryOrchestrator (which will need access to spawn_agent)\\n- The Executive Director spawned for recovery will create a new session or join existing session\\n- Recovery tasks will be visible both in recovery dashboard AND agent hierarchy\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\\n2. Users can track recovery progress the same way they track regular job progress\\n3. Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\\n4. No regression in existing recovery functionality\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BjTJ5DKrRGyB9BSxGB4xEN', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/brass-band-achievements", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/css_accessibility_analysis_report.md", "tests/runtime/agents/test_brass_band_achievements.py"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "84 seconds ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "84 seconds ago"}, {"hash": "a81afe1939da863370999b4c3bff0b885cdea04a", "message": "Executive Director: Complete UI readability fix project for Improve page", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "dbb4e5cdf62e28d6aa04d1d80ad96ffa174e4b4c", "message": "Complete milestone 2: UI readability fix implementation and testing", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "3 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "91abbd5a22e7ab7748eb34750e92010366b3de1f", "message": "Complete milestone 1: UI readability analysis and architecture planning", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "86 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "92d30084e33cc181990ccee0a29990edf61fe10b", "message": "Implement whimsicalNames utility module with arrays, hash function, name generation, and emoji mapping", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "86 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-5-20251101', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.5\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully analyzed the UI readability requirements and designed a focused, practical architecture that addresses the contrast issues without over-engineering. The proposal correctly identifies th...\n- I successfully analyzed the UI readability requirements and designed a focused, practical architecture that addresses the contrast issues without over-engineering. The proposal correctly identifies th...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_s