{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:24:59", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-499e68a8-3309-4406-aa68-8c3788f44bbf', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Recovery Agent System"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01L5VUyP4eAVdkc1Eid4vDSH', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BjTJ5DKrRGyB9BSxGB4xEN', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01L5VUyP4eAVdkc1Eid4vDSH', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Recovery Agent System Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy pane rather than keeping them isolated in the recovery dashboard.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when jobs are recovered through the recovery system:\\n1. Jobs run in a separate recovery context via `RecoveryOrchestrator._retry_agent()`\\n2. Recovered jobs are not visible in the main Agent Hierarchy tree on the Activity view\\n3. The recovery pane shows job status, but jobs may run to completion without appearing in the main UI\\n4. Users cannot track recovered jobs with the same visibility as regular jobs\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a `recovery_agent.md` agent definition in the `leadership/` directory\\n2. Modify the recovery orchestration to spawn Executive Directors via this Recovery Agent for each recovered job\\n3. Ensure recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs\\n4. Maintain visibility into recovery status while integrating with the main workflow\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n- Create a new agent type `leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- The Recovery Agent should:\\n  - Accept recovery task information (failed agent details, failure reason, recovery strategy)\\n  - Spawn an Executive Director to manage the recovered task\\n  - Pass the original user_vision/task to the Executive Director\\n  - Track recovery attempts and escalation history\\n\\n### FR2: Recovery Agent Capabilities\\n- **Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\\n- **Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers or coordinators (must go through Executive Director)\\n- **Input**: Recovery task details from the recovery queue\\n- **Output**: Status of recovery attempt, spawned Executive Director ID\\n\\n### FR3: Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Modify `swarm_recovery.py` to:\\n  - Use spawn_agent tool to spawn Recovery Agent instead of directly calling `_retry_agent`\\n  - Pass necessary context: original input_data, failure reason, recovery strategy\\n  - The Recovery Agent then spawns Executive Director with proper swarm state registration\\n\\n### FR4: Swarm State Integration\\n- Recovered jobs must:\\n  - Register in swarm_state as new agents with proper parent relationships\\n  - Appear in the `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint response\\n  - Be visible in the AgentHierarchyTree component\\n  - Link back to the original failed job via metadata\\n\\n### FR5: UI Visibility\\n- No UI changes required (feature request is backend-focused)\\n- Existing AgentHierarchyTree will automatically show recovered jobs once they\'re in swarm_state\\n- Recovery Dashboard can continue to show recovery-specific status info\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR1: Backward Compatibility\\n- Existing recovery dashboard should continue to work\\n- Recovery queue and history should still be populated\\n\\n### NFR2: Traceability\\n- Each recovery attempt should maintain reference to:\\n  - Original failed agent_id\\n  - Recovery queue entry\\n  - Failure reason and strategy applied\\n\\n## Technical Design Notes\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n    \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - ID of the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"original_session_id\\": \\"string - Session that contained the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"agent_type\\": \\"string - Type of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"agent_name\\": \\"string - Name of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"input_data\\": \\"object - Original input to the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"string - Why the agent failed/stalled\\",\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": \\"integer - Which recovery attempt this is\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"output_directory\\": \\"string - Where to write artifacts\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"recovery_id\\": \\"string - ID of this recovery attempt\\",\\n  \\"spawned_executive_id\\": \\"string - ID of the Executive Director spawned\\",\\n  \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - Reference to original failed agent\\",\\n  \\"message\\": \\"string - Status message\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"string - Performance analysis\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The Recovery Agent will be spawned by the RecoveryOrchestrator (which will need access to spawn_agent)\\n- The Executive Director spawned for recovery will create a new session or join existing session\\n- Recovery tasks will be visible both in recovery dashboard AND agent hierarchy\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\\n2. Users can track recovery progress the same way they track regular job progress\\n3. Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\\n4. No regression in existing recovery functionality\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BjTJ5DKrRGyB9BSxGB4xEN', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/brass-band-achievements", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/css_accessibility_analysis_report.md", "tests/runtime/agents/test_brass_band_achievements.py"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "84 seconds ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "84 seconds ago"}, {"hash": "a81afe1939da863370999b4c3bff0b885cde