{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:25:06", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-57d8a5a0-5d8e-4d27-aefd-10ddd53f6dff', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Recovery Agent System"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011t4vJ84Dw2WjVh4c7T5edZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Gy5tX8D3dfuLQ4jSvJtPmD', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011t4vJ84Dw2WjVh4c7T5edZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Recovery Agent System Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy pane rather than keeping them isolated in the recovery dashboard.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when jobs are recovered through the recovery system:\\n1. Jobs run in a separate recovery context via `RecoveryOrchestrator._retry_agent()`\\n2. Recovered jobs are not visible in the main Agent Hierarchy tree on the Activity view\\n3. The recovery pane shows job status, but jobs may run to completion without appearing in the main UI\\n4. Users cannot track recovered jobs with the same visibility as regular jobs\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a `recovery_agent.md` agent definition in the `leadership/` directory\\n2. Modify the recovery orchestration to spawn Executive Directors via this Recovery Agent for each recovered job\\n3. Ensure recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs\\n4. Maintain visibility into recovery status while integrating with the main workflow\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n- Create a new agent type `leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- The Recovery Agent should:\\n  - Accept recovery task information (failed agent details, failure reason, recovery strategy)\\n  - Spawn an Executive Director to manage the recovered task\\n  - Pass the original user_vision/task to the Executive Director\\n  - Track recovery attempts and escalation history\\n\\n### FR2: Recovery Agent Capabilities\\n- **Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\\n- **Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers or coordinators (must go through Executive Director)\\n- **Input**: Recovery task details from the recovery queue\\n- **Output**: Status of recovery attempt, spawned Executive Director ID\\n\\n### FR3: Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Modify `swarm_recovery.py` to:\\n  - Use spawn_agent tool to spawn Recovery Agent instead of directly calling `_retry_agent`\\n  - Pass necessary context: original input_data, failure reason, recovery strategy\\n  - The Recovery Agent then spawns Executive Director with proper swarm state registration\\n\\n### FR4: Swarm State Integration\\n- Recovered jobs must:\\n  - Register in swarm_state as new agents with proper parent relationships\\n  - Appear in the `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint response\\n  - Be visible in the AgentHierarchyTree component\\n  - Link back to the original failed job via metadata\\n\\n### FR5: UI Visibility\\n- No UI changes required (feature request is backend-focused)\\n- Existing AgentHierarchyTree will automatically show recovered jobs once they\'re in swarm_state\\n- Recovery Dashboard can continue to show recovery-specific status info\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR1: Backward Compatibility\\n- Existing recovery dashboard should continue to work\\n- Recovery queue and history should still be populated\\n\\n### NFR2: Traceability\\n- Each recovery attempt should maintain reference to:\\n  - Original failed agent_id\\n  - Recovery queue entry\\n  - Failure reason and strategy applied\\n\\n## Technical Design Notes\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n    \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - ID of the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"original_session_id\\": \\"string - Session that contained the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"agent_type\\": \\"string - Type of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"agent_name\\": \\"string - Name of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"input_data\\": \\"object - Original input to the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"string - Why the agent failed/stalled\\",\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": \\"integer - Which recovery attempt this is\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"output_directory\\": \\"string - Where to write artifacts\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"recovery_id\\": \\"string - ID of this recovery attempt\\",\\n  \\"spawned_executive_id\\": \\"string - ID of the Executive Director spawned\\",\\n  \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - Reference to original failed agent\\",\\n  \\"message\\": \\"string - Status message\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"string - Performance analysis\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The Recovery Agent will be spawned by the RecoveryOrchestrator (which will need access to spawn_agent)\\n- The Executive Director spawned for recovery will create a new session or join existing session\\n- Recovery tasks will be visible both in recovery dashboard AND agent hierarchy\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\\n2. Users can track recovery progress the same way they track regular job progress\\n3. Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\\n4. No regression in existing recovery functionality\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Gy5tX8D3dfuLQ4jSvJtPmD', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/brass-band-achievements", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/css_accessibility_analysis_report.md", "tests/runtime/agents/test_brass_band_achievements.py"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "56 seconds ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "a8cbbf685ac4792b4535e719c35f0b69d5a00345", "message": "Add diagnostic report for file generation tracking issue - identifies three bugs in activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "56 seconds ago"}, {"hash": "a81afe1939da863370999b4c3bff0b885cdea04a", "message": "Executive Director: Complete UI readability fix project for Improve page", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "dbb4e5cdf62e28d6aa04d1d80ad96ffa174e4b4c", "message": "Complete milestone 2: UI readability fix implementation and testing", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "91abbd5a22e7ab7748eb34750e92010366b3de1f", "message": "Complete milestone 1: UI readability analysis and architecture planning", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "85 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "92d30084e33cc181990ccee0a29990edf61fe10b", "message": "Implement whimsicalNames utility module with arrays, hash function, name generation, and emoji mapping", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "86 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RmJgkiPBBg97ZcWJvesf2V', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Recovery Agent System - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy.\n\n## Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure\n**Duration**: Sprint 1\n**Objective**: Create the Recovery Agent definition and establish the foundation for agent-based recovery\n\n### Deliverables\n1. `leadership/recovery_agent.md` - Agent definition file\n2. Input/output format validation for recovery tasks\n3. Unit tests for Recovery Agent definition parsing\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Recovery Agent definition follows existing agent format patterns\n- [ ] Agent can accept recovery task input format as specified\n- [ ] Agent can spawn Executive Director only (permission enforcement)\n- [ ] Agent outputs match defined output format\n- [ ] Tests pass for agent definition validation\n\n### Dependencies\n- None (foundational milestone)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 2: RecoveryOrchestrator Integration\n**Duration**: Sprint 2\n**Objective**: Modify the recovery orchestration to use the new Recovery Agent\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Modified `swarm_recovery.py` to spawn Recovery Agent\n2. Recovery Agent spawning Executive Director with proper context\n3. Integration tests for the recovery flow\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] RecoveryOrchestrator spawns Recovery Agent instead of direct retry\n- [ ] Recovery Agent successfully spawns Executive Director\n- [ ] Original task context is properly passed through the chain\n- [ ] Recovery attempt tracking is maintained\n- [ ] No regression in existing recovery functionality\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 1 complete (Recovery Agent definition exists)\n\n---\n\n## Milestone 3: Swarm State Integration & Visibility\n**Duration**: Sprint 3\n**Objective**: Ensure recovered jobs appear in the agent hierarchy\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Proper swarm_state registration for recovery-spawned agents\n2. Parent-child relationship mapping for recovered agents\n3. Metadata preservation (original failure, attempt count)\n4. End-to-end integration tests\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Recovered jobs register in swarm_state with proper relationships\n- [ ] `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint includes recovered jobs\n- [ ] AgentHierarchyTree automatically displays recovered jobs\n- [ ] Recovery metadata is preserved and accessible\n- [ ] Original failed agent ID is linked in metadata\n- [ ] All tests pass including end-to-end scenarios\n\n### Dependencies\n- Milestone 2 complete (Recovery Agent can spawn Executive Directors)\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n### Technical Risks\n1. **Swarm State Timing**: Recovery agents must register before children spawn\n   - Mitigation: Ensure synchronous registration in spawn flow\n\n2. **Session Management**: Recovered jobs may need new sessions\n   - Mitigation: Allow flexible session handling in Recovery Agent\n\n3. **Backward Compatibility**: Existing recovery dashboard must continue working\n   - Mitigation: Add new functionality without removing existing hooks\n\n### Dependencies\n- Existing agent definition infrastructure must support new agent type\n- spawn_agent tool must be accessible from RecoveryOrchestrator context\n\n---\n\n## Success Metrics\n1. Recovered jobs visible in Agent Hierarchy (primary goal)\n2. No regression in recovery dashboard functionality\n3. Full traceability from original failure to recovery attempt\n4. All acceptance tests passing\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RmJgkiPBBg97ZcWJvesf2V', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_232429.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_232429.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XiSK3grf8MxswJKioFtUBS', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Recovery Agent System'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XiSK3grf8MxswJKioFtUBS', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Wk1saurh3DxvpN7GRtDvYS', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Recovery Agent System'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Wk1saurh3DxvpN7GRtDvYS', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011mtv4dYmVrXLwFVH4gKjXB', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011mtv4dYmVrXLwFVH4gKjXB', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture Proposal: UI Readability Fix for Improve Page\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis is a **targeted remediation architecture** for fixing text readability issues in the SelfImprovementDashboard component. The approach focuses on CSS specificity corrections and conditional styling improvements rather than a major architectural redesign.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-level styling fix with cascading CSS improvements\\n**Rationale**: This is a focused bug fix that requires minimal changes to preserve existing functionality while solving the specific contrast problem. A surgical approach ensures no unintended side effects.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n**No new technologies required** - this fix works within the existing stack:\\n\\n### Frontend (Existing)\\n- **React** - Component framework (already in use)\\n- **Bootstrap 5** - CSS framework with built-in color system (leveraging existing theme)\\n- **CSS-in-JS/Inline Styles** - Current styling approach in the component\\n\\n### Why This Approach\\n- **Minimal Risk**: Works with existing technology and patterns\\n- **Fast Implementation**: No new dependencies or learning curve\\n- **Maintainable**: Uses Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes for consistency\\n- **Tested**: Bootstrap\'s color combinations are accessibility-tested\\n\\n**Alternatives Considered:**\\n- CSS Modules: Overkill for a single component fix\\n- Styled Components: Would require major refactoring\\n- New CSS Framework: Unnecessary complexity for a readability fix\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Core Component\\n**SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx**\\n- **Current State**: Contains conditional styling that causes contrast issues\\n- **Responsibility**: Display performance analytics with proper text contrast\\n- **Fix Strategy**: Update styling logic to ensure text colors adapt with background changes\\n\\n### Styling Architecture\\n```\\nSelfImprovementDashboard\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Normal Mode Styling (light backgrounds)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-light, text-dark)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (semantic colors with proper text)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (standard contrast)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 \\"Bumpers Off\\" Mode Styling (dark/danger backgrounds)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Card components (bg-danger, text-white)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Badges (light variants with dark text)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Tables (inverted contrast)\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n```\\nUser Interaction \\u2192 Mode State Change \\u2192 Conditional Styling Logic \\u2192 DOM Update \\u2192 Visual Rendering\\n```\\nNo changes to data flow - only styling application logic.\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n**Files to Modify:**\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 SelfImprovementDashboard.jsx  [PRIMARY TARGET]\\n```\\n\\n**Additional Files (if needed):**\\n```\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 dashboard-overrides.css  [IF NEEDED - for complex overrides]\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeHelpers.js  [IF NEEDED - for styling logic extraction]\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n**No database changes required** - this is purely a presentation layer fix.\\n\\n**State Management:**\\n- Existing component state (bumpers mode, performance data) remains unchanged\\n- Only CSS class application logic needs modification\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n**No API changes required** - this fix is entirely frontend styling.\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Process\\n1. **Local Development**: Test fixes in development server\\n2. **Visual Testing**: Verify contrast in both light and dark modes\\n3. **Accessibility Testing**: Use browser dev tools to verify WCAG compliance\\n4. **Cross-Browser Testing**: Ensure fixes work in Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n\\n### Deployment\\n- **Type**: Frontend-only deployment\\n- **Risk Level**: Low (isolated component changes)\\n- **Rollback Strategy**: Git revert of specific styling changes\\n- **Testing Required**: Visual regression testing\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\nNo environment-specific configuration needed - styles apply universally.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Visual Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Manual test cases:\\n1. Load Improve page in normal mode\\n   \\u2192 Verify all text is readable against backgrounds\\n2. Enable \\"Bumpers Off\\" mode  \\n   \\u2192 Verify danger theme maintains text contrast\\n3. Test responsive breakpoints\\n   \\u2192 Ensure readability on mobile/tablet/desktop\\n```\\n\\n### Automated Testing\\n```javascript\\n// Accessibility tests (if jest-axe available):\\ndescribe(\'SelfImprovementDashboard Accessibility\', () => {\\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in normal mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test WCAG compliance\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'meets contrast requirements in bumpers off mode\', async () => {\\n    // Test danger theme compliance\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Browser Testing\\n- **Chrome**: Primary development browser\\n- **Firefox**: Secondary testing\\n- **Safari**: macOS compatibility\\n- **Edge**: Windows compatibility\\n\\n## Specific Technical Implementation\\n\\n### Bootstrap Color Strategy\\n```jsx\\n// Current problematic pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-muted\\">Problem text</span> // This creates dark on dark\\n</Card>\\n\\n// Fixed pattern:\\n<Card bg=\\"dark\\" text=\\"white\\">\\n  <span className=\\"text-light\\">Readable text</span>\\n</Card>\\n```\\n\\n### Conditional Styling Logic\\n```jsx\\nconst getTextClass = (isDangerMode, baseClass) => {\\n  if (isDangerMode) {\\n    return baseClass.includes(\'dark\') ? \'text-white\' : \'text-light\';\\n  }\\n  return baseClass.includes(\'light\') ? \'text-dark\' : \'text-white\';\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Option 1: Complete CSS Framework Migration\\n**Rejected**: Too much risk for a simple contrast fix\\n\\n### Option 2: Custom Design System\\n**Rejected**: Overkill - Bootstrap\'s accessibility features solve this when used correctly\\n\\n### Option 3: JavaScript-based Theme Switching\\n**Rejected**: Adds complexity when CSS classes can solve the issue\\n\\n### Option 4: CSS Variables for Dynamic Theming\\n**Considered**: Good for future scalability, but unnecessary for this focused fix\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Breaking Existing Visual Design\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use Bootstrap\'s semantic color classes\\n- Test both modes thoroughly\\n- Take screenshots for before/after comparison\\n\\n### Risk 2: CSS Specificity Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use inline styles for high specificity when needed\\n- Follow existing patterns in the codebase\\n- Test in actual browser environment\\n\\n### Risk 3: Performance Impact\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- No new CSS files or frameworks\\n- Minimal additional class computations\\n- No impact on bundle size\\n\\n### Risk 4: Cross-Browser Inconsistency\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use standard Bootstrap classes (well-tested across browsers)\\n- Test in multiple browsers\\n- Avoid custom CSS properties that might not be supported\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Design Questions for User Review\\n1. **Color Preference**: Should danger mode use red backgrounds with white text, or prefer orange/yellow for better accessibility?\\n2. **Badge Styling**: For dark badges, prefer white text or switch to light-colored badges with dark text?\\n3. **Table Styling**: In dark mode, prefer inverted table colors or maintain current table style with better text contrast?\\n\\n### Technical Decisions Requiring Input\\n1. **Approach**: Pure inline styling vs. conditional CSS classes?\\n2. **Scope**: Fix only the reported component or audit entire application for similar issues?\\n3. **Testing**: Include automated accessibility tests or rely on manual verification?\\n\\n## Implementation Phases\\n\\n### Phase 1: Immediate Fix (1-2 hours)\\n- Identify and fix the most critical contrast issues\\n- Focus on badges and card text\\n- Test both normal and danger modes\\n\\n### Phase 2: Comprehensive Audit (2-3 hours)\\n- Review all text elements in the component\\n- Ensure WCAG compliance\\n- Add consistent styling patterns\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing and Validation (1 hour)\\n- Cross-browser testing\\n- Accessibility validation\\n- User acceptance testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n1. **Contrast Ratio**: All text meets WCAG 2.1 AA standards (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large)\\n2. **Visual Verification**: User confirms readability issues are resolved\\n3. **No Regression**: All existing functionality works unchanged\\n4. **Performance**: No measurable impact on page load or rendering performance\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n\\n1. **User Approval**: Confirm this architectural approach before implementation\\n2. **Development**: Implement the CSS fixes following this plan\\n3. **Testing**: Execute the testing strategy outlined above\\n4. **Deployment**: Deploy with the low-risk strategy described\\n\\nThis architecture provides a focused, low-risk solution that addresses the specific readability problem while maintaining system stability and existing functionality."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-5-20251101', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD