{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 23:27:01", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9d631b86-600c-442e-bc3c-76bf4d1253ba', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure - Create the recovery_agent.md agent definition file and establish the foundation for agent-based recovery. Includes input/output format validation.",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TuvCsWM3AfkWwdMpKZikPN', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FrzSeDTp6qy6Se5wCo1zmx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TuvCsWM3AfkWwdMpKZikPN', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Architecture: Recovery Agent System\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis architecture introduces a **Recovery Agent** into the agent hierarchy to govern job recovery. The key innovation is replacing direct retry mechanisms with agent-spawned recovery, ensuring recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Agent-based Recovery Orchestration\\n**Rationale**: By treating recovery as a first-class agent-spawned operation, recovered jobs automatically integrate with existing swarm state tracking, hierarchy visualization, and monitoring infrastructure.\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. Recovery Agent (`leadership/recovery_agent.md`)\\n**Role**: Specialized leadership agent that governs recovery operations\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Accept recovery task information from RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Spawn Executive Directors to handle recovered tasks\\n- Track recovery attempts and maintain metadata\\n- Report recovery status back to orchestrator\\n\\n**Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\\n**Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers, coordinators, or other agents\\n\\n### 2. Modified RecoveryOrchestrator (`swarm_recovery.py`)\\n**Role**: Orchestrates recovery queue processing\\n**Changes Required**:\\n- Instead of calling `_retry_agent()` directly, spawn Recovery Agent via `spawn_agent` tool\\n- Pass recovery context (original input, failure reason, strategy) to Recovery Agent\\n- Monitor spawned Recovery Agent for completion\\n\\n### 3. Swarm State Integration\\n**Role**: Existing infrastructure, minimal changes needed\\n**Requirement**: Recovery Agent and its spawned Executive Directors must register properly\\n**Behavior**: Once agents register in swarm_state, they automatically appear in hierarchy API\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502                        CURRENT FLOW (TO BE REPLACED)                     \\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2524\\n\\u2502                                                                          \\u2502\\n\\u2502  RecoveryOrchestrator                                                    \\u2502\\n\\u2502         \\u2502                                                                \\u2502\\n\\u2502         \\u25bc                                                                \\u2502\\n\\u2502  _retry_agent() \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u25ba Direct Agent Spawn                               \\u2502\\n\\u2502         \\u2502                    (No swarm_state registration)               \\u2502\\n\\u2502         \\u25bc                                                                \\u2502\\n\\u2502  Recovery Dashboard Only                                                 \\u2502\\n\\u2502  (Jobs NOT visible in hierarchy)                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                                                          \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n\\n\\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510\\n\\u2502                        NEW FLOW (TO BE IMPLEMENTED)                      \\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2524\\n\\u2502                                                                          \\u2502\\n\\u2502  RecoveryOrchestrator                                                    \\u2502\\n\\u2502         \\u2502                                                                \\u2502\\n\\u2502         \\u2502 spawn_agent(\\"leadership/recovery_agent\\", recovery_task)        \\u2502\\n\\u2502         \\u25bc                                                                \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510                                                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 Recovery Agent  \\u2502 \\u25c4\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500 Registers in swarm_state                      \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502 (leadership/)   \\u2502                                                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u252c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518                                                     \\u2502\\n\\u2502           \\u2502                                                              \\u2502\\n\\u2502           \\u2502 spawn_agent(\\"leadership/executive_director\\", original_task)  \\u2502\\n\\u2502           \\u25bc                                                              \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510                                               \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  Executive Director   \\u2502 \\u25c4\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500 Registers in swarm_state                \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  (recovered task)     \\u2502       Parent: Recovery Agent                  \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u252c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518                                               \\u2502\\n\\u2502           \\u2502                                                              \\u2502\\n\\u2502           \\u25bc (normal ED workflow)                                         \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u250c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2510                                               \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2502  Dev Manager, etc.    \\u2502 \\u25c4\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500 All children visible in hierarchy       \\u2502\\n\\u2502  \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518                                               \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                                                          \\u2502\\n\\u2502  Result: All agents visible in Agent Hierarchy Tree                      \\u2502\\n\\u2502          + Recovery Dashboard still shows recovery-specific info         \\u2502\\n\\u2502                                                                          \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2518\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n### New Files to Create\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 docs/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 agents/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 leadership/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 recovery_agent.md    # New agent definition\\n```\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 runtime/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 swarm_recovery.py    # Use spawn_agent instead of direct retry\\n```\\n\\n### No Changes Required\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 field/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ensemble_ui/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 activity.py   # Hierarchy endpoint already works\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n            \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n                \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n                    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AgentHierarchyTree.jsx  # Already displays swarm_state\\n```\\n\\n## Recovery Agent Definition\\n\\n### Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n    \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - ID of the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"original_session_id\\": \\"string - Session that contained the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"agent_type\\": \\"string - Type of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"agent_name\\": \\"string - Name of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"input_data\\": \\"object - Original input to the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"string - Why the agent failed/stalled\\",\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": \\"integer - Which recovery attempt this is\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"output_directory\\": \\"string - Where to write artifacts\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"recovery_id\\": \\"string - ID of this recovery attempt\\",\\n  \\"spawned_executive_id\\": \\"string - ID of the Executive Director spawned\\",\\n  \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - Reference to original failed agent\\",\\n  \\"message\\": \\"string - Status message\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"string - Performance analysis\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Agent Definition Structure\\n```markdown\\n# Recovery Agent\\n\\n## Purpose\\nGoverns job recovery by spawning Executive Directors for recovered tasks.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Receive recovery task from RecoveryOrchestrator\\n2. Extract original input_data and task context\\n3. Spawn Executive Director with original task + recovery metadata\\n4. Monitor Executive Director completion\\n5. Report recovery status\\n\\n## Permissions\\n- can_spawn: [\\"leadership/executive_director\\"]\\n- can_write_code: false\\n\\n## Input Format\\n(as above)\\n\\n## Output Format\\n(as above)\\n```\\n\\n## API Changes\\n\\n### No New Endpoints Required\\nThe existing `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint will automatically include recovered jobs once they register in swarm_state.\\n\\n### Metadata Enhancement\\nRecovery-spawned agents should include metadata:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"agent_id\\": \\"recovery-exec-abc123\\",\\n  \\"agent_type\\": \\"leadership/executive_director\\",\\n  \\"metadata\\": {\\n    \\"is_recovery\\": true,\\n    \\"original_failed_agent_id\\": \\"original-abc123\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": 1,\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"retry\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"timeout\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Integration Points\\n\\n### RecoveryOrchestrator Changes\\n```python\\n# BEFORE (swarm_recovery.py)\\nasync def _process_recovery_task(self, task):\\n    await self._retry_agent(task)  # Direct retry, no hierarchy integration\\n\\n# AFTER\\nasync def _process_recovery_task(self, task):\\n    recovery_input = {\\n        \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n            \\"original_agent_id\\": task.agent_id,\\n            \\"original_session_id\\": task.session_id,\\n            \\"agent_type\\": task.agent_type,\\n            \\"agent_name\\": task.agent_name,\\n            \\"input_data\\": task.input_data,\\n            \\"failure_reason\\": task.failure_reason,\\n            \\"recovery_strategy\\": task.recovery_strategy,\\n            \\"recovery_attempt\\": task.attempt_count\\n        },\\n        \\"output_directory\\": self.output_directory\\n    }\\n    \\n    # Spawn Recovery Agent (which spawns ED, which registers in swarm_state)\\n    result = await self.spawn_agent(\\n        \\"leadership/recovery_agent\\",\\n        recovery_input\\n    )\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Tests\\n1. Recovery Agent definition parsing\\n2. Input/output format validation\\n3. Permission enforcement (can only spawn ED)\\n\\n### Integration Tests\\n1. RecoveryOrchestrator \\u2192 Recovery Agent spawning\\n2. Recovery Agent \\u2192 Executive Director spawning\\n3. Swarm state registration verification\\n\\n### End-to-End Tests\\n1. Trigger a recoverable failure\\n2. Verify job enters recovery queue\\n3. Verify Recovery Agent spawns\\n4. Verify Executive Director appears in hierarchy\\n5. Verify recovery metadata preserved\\n\\n## Backward Compatibility\\n\\n### Preserved Functionality\\n- Recovery queue continues to work\\n- Recovery dashboard continues to show recovery status\\n- Recovery history is still populated\\n- Existing UI components unchanged\\n\\n### New Behavior\\n- Recovered jobs NOW also appear in Agent Hierarchy\\n- Recovery metadata available in hierarchy view\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: spawn_agent Availability\\n**Issue**: RecoveryOrchestrator may not have access to spawn_agent tool\\n**Mitigation**: Ensure RecoveryOrchestrator runs in a context with tool access, or create a spawning utility\\n\\n### Risk 2: Session Management\\n**Issue**: Recovered jobs may create orphaned sessions\\n**Mitigation**: Recovery Agent should reuse existing session or create with proper parent reference\\n\\n### Risk 3: Infinite Recovery Loops\\n**Issue**: Recovery Agent could fail, triggering more recovery\\n**Mitigation**: Mark Recovery Agent as non-recoverable or add loop detection\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\\n2. \\u2705 Users can track recovery progress the same way as regular jobs\\n3. \\u2705 Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\\n4. \\u2705 No regression in existing recovery functionality\\n5. \\u2705 All tests pass\\n\\n## Open Questions (None - Decisions Made)\\n\\n1. **Session handling**: Recovery Agent creates new session linked to recovery queue entry\\n2. **Recovery Agent failures**: Mark Recovery Agent as non-recoverable to prevent loops\\n3. **UI changes**: None required - existing UI auto-displays registered agents\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FrzSeDTp6qy6Se5wCo1zmx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Recovery Agent System Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nCreate a Recovery Agent that governs job recovery by spawning Executive Directors to manage the recovery of each job, integrating recovered jobs back into the main agent hierarchy pane rather than keeping them isolated in the recovery dashboard.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nCurrently, when jobs are recovered through the recovery system:\\n1. Jobs run in a separate recovery context via `RecoveryOrchestrator._retry_agent()`\\n2. Recovered jobs are not visible in the main Agent Hierarchy tree on the Activity view\\n3. The recovery pane shows job status, but jobs may run to completion without appearing in the main UI\\n4. Users cannot track recovered jobs with the same visibility as regular jobs\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Create a `recovery_agent.md` agent definition in the `leadership/` directory\\n2. Modify the recovery orchestration to spawn Executive Directors via this Recovery Agent for each recovered job\\n3. Ensure recovered jobs appear in the main agent hierarchy alongside regular jobs\\n4. Maintain visibility into recovery status while integrating with the main workflow\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### FR1: Recovery Agent Definition\\n- Create a new agent type `leadership/recovery_agent.md`\\n- The Recovery Agent should:\\n  - Accept recovery task information (failed agent details, failure reason, recovery strategy)\\n  - Spawn an Executive Director to manage the recovered task\\n  - Pass the original user_vision/task to the Executive Director\\n  - Track recovery attempts and escalation history\\n\\n### FR2: Recovery Agent Capabilities\\n- **Can Spawn**: Executive Director only\\n- **Cannot Spawn**: Direct code writers or coordinators (must go through Executive Director)\\n- **Input**: Recovery task details from the recovery queue\\n- **Output**: Status of recovery attempt, spawned Executive Director ID\\n\\n### FR3: Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\\n- Modify `swarm_recovery.py` to:\\n  - Use spawn_agent tool to spawn Recovery Agent instead of directly calling `_retry_agent`\\n  - Pass necessary context: original input_data, failure reason, recovery strategy\\n  - The Recovery Agent then spawns Executive Director with proper swarm state registration\\n\\n### FR4: Swarm State Integration\\n- Recovered jobs must:\\n  - Register in swarm_state as new agents with proper parent relationships\\n  - Appear in the `/api/activity/hierarchy` endpoint response\\n  - Be visible in the AgentHierarchyTree component\\n  - Link back to the original failed job via metadata\\n\\n### FR5: UI Visibility\\n- No UI changes required (feature request is backend-focused)\\n- Existing AgentHierarchyTree will automatically show recovered jobs once they\'re in swarm_state\\n- Recovery Dashboard can continue to show recovery-specific status info\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### NFR1: Backward Compatibility\\n- Existing recovery dashboard should continue to work\\n- Recovery queue and history should still be populated\\n\\n### NFR2: Traceability\\n- Each recovery attempt should maintain reference to:\\n  - Original failed agent_id\\n  - Recovery queue entry\\n  - Failure reason and strategy applied\\n\\n## Technical Design Notes\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Input Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"recovery_task\\": {\\n    \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - ID of the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"original_session_id\\": \\"string - Session that contained the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"agent_type\\": \\"string - Type of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"agent_name\\": \\"string - Name of agent that failed\\",\\n    \\"input_data\\": \\"object - Original input to the failed agent\\",\\n    \\"failure_reason\\": \\"string - Why the agent failed/stalled\\",\\n    \\"recovery_strategy\\": \\"string - Strategy to apply (retry, enhance_prompt, etc.)\\",\\n    \\"recovery_attempt\\": \\"integer - Which recovery attempt this is\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"output_directory\\": \\"string - Where to write artifacts\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Recovery Agent Output Format\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success|failed|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"recovery_id\\": \\"string - ID of this recovery attempt\\",\\n  \\"spawned_executive_id\\": \\"string - ID of the Executive Director spawned\\",\\n  \\"original_agent_id\\": \\"string - Reference to original failed agent\\",\\n  \\"message\\": \\"string - Status message\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"string - Performance analysis\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The Recovery Agent will be spawned by the RecoveryOrchestrator (which will need access to spawn_agent)\\n- The Executive Director spawned for recovery will create a new session or join existing session\\n- Recovery tasks will be visible both in recovery dashboard AND agent hierarchy\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. When a job is recovered, it appears in the main Agent Hierarchy tree\\n2. Users can track recovery progress the same way they track regular job progress\\n3. Recovery metadata (attempt count, original failure) is preserved\\n4. No regression in existing recovery functionality\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LabqF7xAdx8WKbe5U5r4Fs', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Backend Tasks - Milestone 1: Recovery Agent Definition & Core Infrastructure\n\n## Overview\nThis milestone establishes the foundation for agent-based recovery by creating the Recovery Agent definition and implementing input/output format validation. This is the foundational work that enables recovered jobs to appear in the main agent hierarchy.\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 1: Recovery Agent Definition\n\n### Task 1.1: Create Recovery Agent Definition File\n**Description**: Create the `recovery_agent.md` agent definition file in the leadership directory following the standard agent definition format.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- File created at `src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership/recovery_agent.md`\n- Contains all required sections: Purpose, Instructions, Permissions, Input Format, Output Format, Termination Conditions\n- Input format matches specification (recovery_task object + output_directory)\n- Output format matches specification (status, recovery_id, spawned_executive_id, etc.)\n- Permissions explicitly set: `can_spawn: ["leadership/executive_director"]`, `can_write_code: false`, `can_write_tests: false`\n- Instructions clearly define: receive recovery task → spawn Executive Director → monitor completion → report status\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Follow existing agent definition patterns from `docs/agents/leadership/`\n- Include recovery-specific workflow steps\n- Document error handling expectations\n- Specify metadata requirements for recovery tracking\n\n---\n\n### Task 1.2: Create Recovery Agent Input Validation Schema\n**Description**: Create Pydantic models for validating Recovery Agent input format, ensuring all required fields are present and correctly typed.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryTaskInput` created for the recovery_task object\n- Fields validated: original_agent_id (str), original_session_id (str), agent_type (str), agent_name (str), input_data (dict), failure_reason (str), recovery_strategy (str), recovery_attempt (int)\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryAgentInput` created wrapping recovery_task + output_directory\n- Validation includes: required field checks, type validation, string min/max lengths where appropriate\n- All validation errors return clear messages indicating which field failed and why\n- Unit tests cover: valid input, missing fields, wrong types, invalid values\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1 (definition file provides specification)\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Create in `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py` (new file)\n- Use Pydantic v2 syntax with Field validators\n- recovery_strategy should be an enum: ["retry", "enhance_prompt", "escalate"]\n- recovery_attempt must be positive integer\n- input_data is dict with no schema (flexible for any agent type)\n\n---\n\n### Task 1.3: Create Recovery Agent Output Validation Schema\n**Description**: Create Pydantic models for validating Recovery Agent output format, ensuring consistent response structure.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Pydantic model `RecoveryAgentOutput` created\n- Fields validated: status (enum: success/failed/needs_user_input), recovery_id (str), spawned_executive_id (str), original_agent_id (str), message (str), self_analysis (str)\n- All fields required except self_analysis (optional)\n- Status enum properly defined and enforced\n- Unit tests cover: valid output, missing fields, invalid status values\n- Output validation integrated with agent response handling\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1 (definition file provides specification)\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Add to `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py`\n- Status enum: `RecoveryStatus = Literal["success", "failed", "needs_user_input"]`\n- recovery_id and spawned_executive_id should follow UUID format (add validator)\n- self_analysis defaults to empty string if not provided\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 2: Validation Infrastructure\n\n### Task 2.1: Create Validation Utility for Agent I/O\n**Description**: Create a generic utility function that validates agent inputs and outputs against their defined schemas, usable by the Recovery Agent and future agents.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Function `validate_agent_input(agent_type: str, input_data: dict) -> tuple[bool, dict|str]` created\n- Function `validate_agent_output(agent_type: str, output_data: dict) -> tuple[bool, dict|str]` created\n- Functions return (success: bool, validated_data_or_error_message)\n- Schema registry maps agent types to their Pydantic models\n- Recovery Agent schemas registered in the registry\n- Unit tests cover: valid data, invalid data, unknown agent type, malformed JSON\n- Error messages are descriptive and actionable\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2, Task 1.3\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Create `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/agent_validator.py` (new file)\n- Schema registry: `AGENT_SCHEMAS = {"leadership/recovery_agent": {"input": RecoveryAgentInput, "output": RecoveryAgentOutput}}`\n- Handle Pydantic ValidationError and return formatted error messages\n- Cache schema instances for performance\n- Future-proof: allow dynamic schema registration\n\n---\n\n### Task 2.2: Integrate Validation into Agent Spawn Pipeline\n**Description**: Hook the validation utility into the agent spawning process so that input validation occurs before spawning and output validation occurs after completion.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- `spawn_agent` function validates input using `validate_agent_input` before spawning\n- If validation fails, spawn_agent returns error without spawning agent\n- Agent completion handler validates output using `validate_agent_output`\n- If output validation fails, log warning but don\'t block (agent already completed)\n- Validation errors logged with agent_type, input/output data, and specific validation failure\n- Integration tests verify validation occurs at correct points in lifecycle\n- Metrics tracked: validation_failures_total (by agent_type, validation_type: input/output)\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Modify `src/ensemble/runtime/agent_spawner.py` (or equivalent spawning logic)\n- Add validation call before `Agent.create()` or equivalent\n- Add validation call in agent completion callback/handler\n- Use existing logging infrastructure for validation errors\n- Consider: Add `skip_validation=False` parameter for backwards compatibility during rollout\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 3: Testing Infrastructure\n\n### Task 3.1: Create Recovery Agent Test Fixtures\n**Description**: Create pytest fixtures and test data generators for Recovery Agent testing.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Fixture `valid_recovery_task_input()` generates valid RecoveryAgentInput\n- Fixture `invalid_recovery_task_input(field: str)` generates input with specified invalid field\n- Fixture `valid_recovery_agent_output()` generates valid RecoveryAgentOutput\n- Test data includes edge cases: very long strings, special characters, boundary integers\n- Fixtures parameterizable (e.g., override specific fields)\n- Documentation explains how to use fixtures in tests\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2, Task 1.3\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Create `tests/fixtures/recovery_agent_fixtures.py`\n- Use factory pattern: `def recovery_task_factory(**overrides) -> dict`\n- Include fixtures for all recovery strategies\n- Include fixtures for all status values\n- Ensure generated UUIDs are valid format\n\n---\n\n### Task 3.2: Create Validation Test Suite\n**Description**: Comprehensive test suite for input/output validation covering all schemas and edge cases.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Test file `tests/unit/test_recovery_validation.py` created\n- Tests for RecoveryTaskInput: valid input, each required field missing, each field wrong type, boundary values\n- Tests for RecoveryAgentInput: valid input, missing output_directory, invalid paths\n- Tests for RecoveryAgentOutput: valid output, each status value, missing required fields, invalid UUIDs\n- Tests for validate_agent_input: valid, invalid, unknown agent type, malformed data\n- Tests for validate_agent_output: valid, invalid, unknown agent type\n- All tests pass with >95% code coverage on validation modules\n- Tests use fixtures from Task 3.1\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1, Task 2.1\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Use pytest parametrize for testing multiple invalid field scenarios\n- Test error messages are descriptive\n- Test that Pydantic validation errors are properly caught and formatted\n- Test edge cases: empty strings, null values, extremely large integers\n\n---\n\n### Task 3.3: Create Integration Test for Agent Spawn Validation\n**Description**: Integration test verifying validation occurs correctly during the agent spawn lifecycle.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Test file `tests/integration/test_spawn_validation.py` created\n- Test: Valid input passes validation and agent spawns successfully\n- Test: Invalid input fails validation and agent does not spawn\n- Test: Valid output passes validation silently\n- Test: Invalid output logs warning but doesn\'t block\n- Test: Unknown agent type skips validation (no schema registered)\n- Mock agent spawning to avoid full agent execution\n- Verify validation metrics are incremented correctly\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.2, Task 3.1\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Use pytest-mock for mocking spawn_agent internals\n- Mock agent completion to control output validation testing\n- Capture logs and verify validation error messages appear\n- Mock metrics/telemetry and assert validation_failures_total incremented\n- Test both sync and async spawn paths if applicable\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 4: Documentation & Examples\n\n### Task 4.1: Create Recovery Agent Usage Documentation\n**Description**: Write documentation explaining how to use the Recovery Agent, including input/output examples and integration guidance.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Documentation file `docs/recovery_agent_usage.md` created\n- Sections: Overview, Input Format (with examples), Output Format (with examples), Common Errors, Integration with RecoveryOrchestrator\n- Includes complete JSON examples of valid input and output\n- Documents all recovery strategies and when to use each\n- Explains error messages and how to fix validation failures\n- Links to agent definition file and validation schemas\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1, Task 1.2, Task 1.3\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Use real examples from test fixtures\n- Include code snippets showing how to spawn Recovery Agent\n- Add flowchart showing Recovery Agent workflow\n- Include troubleshooting section with common validation errors\n\n---\n\n### Task 4.2: Create Validation Schema Documentation\n**Description**: Write developer documentation for the validation infrastructure, enabling other agents to adopt validation.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Documentation file `docs/agent_validation.md` created\n- Sections: Overview, Creating Schemas, Registering Schemas, Testing Validation, Best Practices\n- Step-by-step guide for adding validation to new agent types\n- Example showing full validation implementation for a sample agent\n- Documents the validation utility API\n- Explains validation timing (pre-spawn, post-completion)\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1, Task 2.2\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Include code examples for creating Pydantic schemas\n- Show how to register schemas in AGENT_SCHEMAS registry\n- Document when to use strict vs lenient validation\n- Explain error handling patterns\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Total Tasks**: 11\n**Task Groups**: 4\n\n**Dependencies Chain**:\n1. Foundation: Task 1.1 (agent definition)\n2. Schemas: Task 1.2, 1.3 (input/output schemas)\n3. Validation Infrastructure: Task 2.1 → Task 2.2 (validation utilities → integration)\n4. Testing: Task 3.1 → Task 3.2, Task 3.3 (fixtures → tests)\n5. Documentation: Task 4.1, Task 4.2 (parallel, depend on implementation tasks)\n\n**Critical Path**: \nTask 1.1 → Task 1.2 → Task 2.1 → Task 2.2 → Task 3.3\n\n**Estimated Complexity**:\n- Simple: 4 tasks\n- Medium: 6 tasks\n- Complex: 0 tasks\n\n**Key Deliverables**:\n1. `src/ensemble/docs/agents/leadership/recovery_agent.md` - Agent definition\n2. `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/recovery_schemas.py` - Pydantic validation models\n3. `src/ensemble/runtime/validation/agent_validator.py` - Validation utility\n4. Integration with spawn pipeline for automatic validation\n5. Comprehensive test suite with >95% coverage\n6. Developer documentation for recovery agent and validation infrastructure\n\n**Ready for Handoff**: Yes - All tasks are well-defined, have clear acceptance criteria, and can be implemented via TDD by the TDD Coordinator.\n'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LabqF7xAdx8WKbe5U5r4Fs', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260114_232701.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1_20260114_232701.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929', 'system': 'You are a Backend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks backend milestones into specific API, database, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify backend components, endpoints, data models, and business logic. Coordinates backend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break backend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Backend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**API Style**: REST with JSON, OpenAPI docs\n**Framework**: FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js)\n**Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy/Prisma ORM\n**Auth**: JWT tokens, bcrypt password hashing\n**Validation**: Pydantic (Python) or Joi (Node.js)\n**Testing**: pytest or Jest with coverage\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all backend components:\n  * API endpoints (REST, GraphQL)\n  * Database models/schemas\n  * Business logic services\n  * Authentication/authorization\n  * Background jobs/workers\n  * External API integrations\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (how to know it\'s done)\nDependencies (what must be done first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by Priority**\nGroup related tasks together\nOrder by dependencies (foundational → features)\nIdentify critical path tasks\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Backend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Business logic is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "calculate shipping" without formula)\n- **Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., sync vs async processing)\n- **Data relationships are contradictory** (e.g., conflicting schema requirements)\n- **Security/compliance requirements are ambiguous** (e.g., PII handling rules)\n- **NOT for**: standard tech choices, common patterns, typical implementations\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All backend tasks identified and documented\n- Task dependencies mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.7\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
